{"parentUuid":"3ec5de02-74d9-4df4-b095-d8527f484ad7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgExThKAui8u71D16Df7R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The measurements reveal three wins: culling off-screen enemies, a low-detail soldier mesh for distant units, and a thinned mid-distance tree model — plus I'll add automatic resolution scaling for weaker GPUs/high-DPI screens. Starting the two Blender asset jobs in the background now, then moving to the engine-side culling work.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2412,"cache_read_input_tokens":566889,"output_tokens":9391,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7556},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2412,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9391,"cache_read_input_tokens":566889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2412},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"541e1b02-56b7-4721-bbea-dee62dc32d7c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgExTgfEhLbzNyxB8SAJR","requestRef":"a7b47c9b-8719-4d7c-a342-7e248153691e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"Claude Browser","attributionMcpTool":"javascript_tool","type":"assistant","uuid":"2e69b8f2-f318-47bf-ac59-b5a767d4064a","timestamp":"2026-10-21T07:06:18.077Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"2e69b8f2-f318-47bf-ac59-b5a767d4064a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgExThKAui8u71D16Df7R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ByWBUZzcMsG5F8hDqBV8Ep","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ae51200f68617c8f0","summary":"Add distant LOD meshes to the soldiers","message":"New soldier task (performance): add a low-detail LOD mesh per outfit to soldier.glb. Profiling shows each in-view enemy costs a 29k-tri skinned + 3-morph mesh even at 100 m; ~20 are in view at once in the village.\n\nAdd `allied_lod` and `axis_lod`: skinned mesh nodes, children of `rig`, bound to the SAME skin (same 20 joints and inverse bind matrices as the full meshes), using the SAME glTF material as the full mesh of that outfit (`allied` / `axis` — share the material and its images, do not duplicate textures). Target ~5–6k tris each, made from the final baked/UV'd mesh by decimation that preserves UV seams and boundaries (so the baked texture maps exactly), keeps the silhouette (helmet, shoulders, webbing, pack, boots; arms and hands still readable for aiming poses), no interior/hidden parts. Skin weights ≤4 per vertex, normalised (transfer from the full skinned mesh, interpolated), COLOR_0 kept (flat white is fine), NO morph targets. Everything else stays exactly as now: full meshes, morph targets and their order, rig, bones, clips, reload_events, sockets, node names; weapons.glb byte-identical (restore it if the build re-exports). soldier.glb ≤ 7 MB (it is 6.30 MB now). Deterministic.\n\nNote: I am about to run a nature build in parallel (mid-distance tree LODs), so your bake will share the CPU; don't start a second soldier build while one runs. No commits, no browser, no server; don't edit kit.py/bake.py/surfaces.py/JS.\n\nVerify by script (both LOD nodes: parent `rig`, skin index same as the full mesh's, material index same as the full mesh's, tris, weights, no targets; everything else unchanged vs the current GLB — keep a copy of the current soldier.glb to compare). Render previews: full vs LOD side by side for both outfits at 10 m and 30 m in rest, aim, run and death_fwd; look at them. Run the five node checks. Update notes/soldier.md (v4.2) and the MODELS.md soldier row. Report tris per LOD, file size, and anything that looks wrong.","type":"message","recipient":"ae51200f68617c8f0","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"New soldier task (performance): add a low-detail …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2412,"cache_read_input_tokens":566889,"output_tokens":9391,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7556},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2412,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9391,"cache_read_input_tokens":566889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2412},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01ByWBUZzcMsG5F8hDqBV8Ep":{"to":"ae51200f68617c8f0","summary":"Add distant LOD meshes to the soldiers","message":"New soldier task (performance): add a low-detail LOD mesh per outfit to soldier.glb. Profiling shows each in-view enemy costs a 29k-tri skinned + 3-morph mesh even at 100 m; ~20 are in view at once in the village.\n\nAdd `allied_lod` and `axis_lod`: skinned mesh nodes, children of `rig`, bound to the SAME skin (same 20 joints and inverse bind matrices as the full meshes), using the SAME glTF material as the full mesh of that outfit (`allied` / `axis` — share the material and its images, do not duplicate textures). Target ~5–6k tris each, made from the final baked/UV'd mesh by decimation that preserves UV seams and boundaries (so the baked texture maps exactly), keeps the silhouette (helmet, shoulders, webbing, pack, boots; arms and hands still readable for aiming poses), no interior/hidden parts. Skin weights ≤4 per vertex, normalised (transfer from the full skinned mesh, interpolated), COLOR_0 kept (flat white is fine), NO morph targets. Everything else stays exactly as now: full meshes, morph targets and their order, rig, bones, clips, reload_events, sockets, node names; weapons.glb byte-identical (restore it if the build re-exports). soldier.glb ≤ 7 MB (it is 6.30 MB now). Deterministic.\n\nNote: I am about to run a nature build in parallel (mid-distance tree LODs), so your bake will share the CPU; don't start a second soldier build while one runs. No commits, no browser, no server; don't edit kit.py/bake.py/surfaces.py/JS.\n\nVerify by script (both LOD nodes: parent `rig`, skin index same as the full mesh's, material index same as the full mesh's, tris, weights, no targets; everything else unchanged vs the current GLB — keep a copy of the current soldier.glb to compare). Render previews: full vs LOD side by side for both outfits at 10 m and 30 m in rest, aim, run and death_fwd; look at them. Run the five node checks. Update notes/soldier.md (v4.2) and the MODELS.md soldier row. Report tris per LOD, file size, and anything that looks wrong."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"541e1b02-56b7-4721-bbea-dee62dc32d7c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgExTgfEhLbzNyxB8SAJR","requestRef":"a7b47c9b-8719-4d7c-a342-7e248153691e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"Claude Browser","attributionMcpTool":"javascript_tool","type":"assistant","uuid":"3115e791-c7ec-4776-81c8-bf25b095862b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T07:06:23.824Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"3115e791-c7ec-4776-81c8-bf25b095862b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgExThKAui8u71D16Df7R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Knncw1T28zKQWc58yrBc3t","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a7113d61792f1e069","summary":"Add mid-distance tree LODs to nature","message":"New nature task (performance), from the user's \"improve performance\" request. In the browser the forest view spends ~2 ms of GPU per frame on the full trees inside the 52 m near range (pine_big/fir_big ~7.8k tris, others 3.7–5.2k, a few hundred in range), and the near→impostor swap can't move closer without visible popping. So the engine will get a third tier: full model up to ~22–28 m, a new MID model from there to the near limit (~52 m), the existing `_lod` impostor beyond.\n\nAdd a `<name>_mid` node for every tree that has a `_lod`: pine_a, pine_b, pine_c, oak_a, oak_b, birch_a, tree_dead, pine_big, fir_big, oak_big, beech_big.\n- Same origin, orientation and scale as the full node; visual only (no colliders/anchors needed).\n- About 25–30 % of the full tris: trunk and main limbs decimated keeping the silhouette, fine twigs dropped; leaf/needle cards thinned to ~35–45 % of the count but enlarged (~1.3–1.5×, area-preserving) so crown coverage, density, colour and silhouette match the full tree from 25–55 m. Cards keep their crown-out normals and stay alphaMode MASK.\n- Reuse the existing materials and atlases (the full tree's bark material, the shared card atlases) — do not duplicate images. Every primitive keeps POSITION/NORMAL/TEXCOORD_0/COLOR_0 (card occlusion in COLOR_0 as now).\n- nature.glb ≤ 16 MB (13.4 MB now). Deterministic. Everything else unchanged (all existing nodes byte-for-byte equivalent in geometry/materials/extras).\n\nNote: a soldier build is running in parallel, so bakes share the CPU. No commits, no browser, no server; don't edit kit.py/bake.py/surfaces.py/JS.\n\nVerify by script (every `_mid` node present, tris vs full, materials shared, attributes, alpha modes; existing nodes unchanged — keep a copy of the current nature.glb to compare). Previews: full vs mid side by side at 30 m and 45 m for each tree, in dim dusk-like light, plus a forest scene; look at them and iterate so the swap at ~25 m would be hard to notice. fix_card_alpha runs in the build. Run the five node checks. Update notes/nature.md and the MODELS.md nature row. Report the tris per mid node, file size, and anything that doesn't land.","type":"message","recipient":"a7113d61792f1e069","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"New nature task (performance), from the user's \"i…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2412,"cache_read_input_tokens":566889,"output_tokens":9391,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7556},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2412,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9391,"cache_read_input_tokens":566889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2412},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Knncw1T28zKQWc58yrBc3t":{"to":"a7113d61792f1e069","summary":"Add mid-distance tree LODs to nature","message":"New nature task (performance), from the user's \"improve performance\" request. In the browser the forest view spends ~2 ms of GPU per frame on the full trees inside the 52 m near range (pine_big/fir_big ~7.8k tris, others 3.7–5.2k, a few hundred in range), and the near→impostor swap can't move closer without visible popping. So the engine will get a third tier: full model up to ~22–28 m, a new MID model from there to the near limit (~52 m), the existing `_lod` impostor beyond.\n\nAdd a `<name>_mid` node for every tree that has a `_lod`: pine_a, pine_b, pine_c, oak_a, oak_b, birch_a, tree_dead, pine_big, fir_big, oak_big, beech_big.\n- Same origin, orientation and scale as the full node; visual only (no colliders/anchors needed).\n- About 25–30 % of the full tris: trunk and main limbs decimated keeping the silhouette, fine twigs dropped; leaf/needle cards thinned to ~35–45 % of the count but enlarged (~1.3–1.5×, area-preserving) so crown coverage, density, colour and silhouette match the full tree from 25–55 m. Cards keep their crown-out normals and stay alphaMode MASK.\n- Reuse the existing materials and atlases (the full tree's bark material, the shared card atlases) — do not duplicate images. Every primitive keeps POSITION/NORMAL/TEXCOORD_0/COLOR_0 (card occlusion in COLOR_0 as now).\n- nature.glb ≤ 16 MB (13.4 MB now). Deterministic. Everything else unchanged (all existing nodes byte-for-byte equivalent in geometry/materials/extras).\n\nNote: a soldier build is running in parallel, so bakes share the CPU. No commits, no browser, no server; don't edit kit.py/bake.py/surfaces.py/JS.\n\nVerify by script (every `_mid` node present, tris vs full, materials shared, attributes, alpha modes; existing nodes unchanged — keep a copy of the current nature.glb to compare). Previews: full vs mid side by side at 30 m and 45 m for each tree, in dim dusk-like light, plus a forest scene; look at them and iterate so the swap at ~25 m would be hard to notice. fix_card_alpha runs in the build. Run the five node checks. Update notes/nature.md and the MODELS.md nature row. Report the tris per mid node, file size, and anything that doesn't land."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"541e1b02-56b7-4721-bbea-dee62dc32d7c","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgExTgfEhLbzNyxB8SAJR","requestRef":"a7b47c9b-8719-4d7c-a342-7e248153691e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5",