{"parentUuid":"f57873e4-56b6-45c3-a5e4-f944bc0b6f64","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEy37dqEuQjH6raoci2G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E7eDPWcGBJhLuTyvheohmh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 50,80p README.md; sed -n 96,125p README.md","description":"Read the README module list and test section"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":584,"cache_read_input_tokens":617648,"output_tokens":147,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":584,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":147,"cache_read_input_tokens":617648,"cache_creation_input_tokens":584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":584},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01E7eDPWcGBJhLuTyvheohmh":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow && sed -n 50,80p README.md; sed -n 96,125p README.md","description":"Read the README module list and test section"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01E7eDPWcGBJhLuTyvheohmh":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"924d5d5c-ca77-49d9-b20e-a90c62de5ba1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEy37DXh4BTq7nFqeVrQ","requestRef":"f71319a5-a362-48c5-8914-8365e1e69366","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"498b79f2-4ae6-4d8b-9755-5d48507abcd7","timestamp":"2026-10-21T07:12:29.321Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"498b79f2-4ae6-4d8b-9755-5d48507abcd7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f2931d76-f215-48b0-832c-a4841c52823c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E7eDPWcGBJhLuTyvheohmh","type":"tool_result","content":"gun reloads by itself after the last round. The enemy reloads too — five\nrounds for a Kar98k, 32 for an MP 40, a 75-round belt for the MG 42 — and\nducks while he does. The dead fall as ragdolls, pushed by the shot or thrown\nby the blast that killed them, and drop their rifles.\n\n## How it is built\n\n* `js/` — three.js r185 (the site's vendored copy), plain ES modules, no build.\n  * `main.js` boot, menus, frame loop · `levelBuild.js` level data → world ·\n    `levels/saint-clair.js` the mission (ground, props, enemies, objectives)\n  * `terrain.js` heightfield + splat material · `world.js` colliders, rays,\n    walking · `vegetation.js` instanced trees and ground cover with LOD\n  * `player.js`, `camera.js`, `character.js` (rig, split upper/lower body\n    animation), `ragdoll.js` (Verlet bodies driving the bones), `combat.js`\n    (hit volumes, grenades, charges, dropped magazines and rifles), `ai.js`\n    (perception, cover, MG nests, sniper, reloads), `mission.js`\n  * `distance.js` the countryside beyond the level: a terrain ring of fields\n    and woods to ~1 km with thousands of far-LOD trees, copses on the far\n    hills, rings of layered treeline cards on the horizon (150–350 m, facing\n    the level, open towards the far buildings) and the next village\n  * `materials.js` palette-keyed wet materials · `sky.js`, `weather.js`\n    (rain, splashes, lightning), `lights.js` (pooled point lights),\n    `effects.js` (particles), `atmosphere.js` (halos, mist, decals),\n    `post.js` + `bloom.js`, `audio.js` (procedural)\n* `assets/models/*.glb` — built by the Blender scripts in `tools/blender/`;\n  see `assets/models/MODELS.md` (pipeline, sizes, build commands),\n  `tools/blender/notes/` (every node) and `docs/models-brief*.md`:\n\n      /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender --background --factory-startup \\\n          --python fun/hedgerow/tools/blender/build_<set>.py\n      python3 -I fun/hedgerow/tools/fix_card_alpha.py fun/hedgerow/assets/models/{village,military,nature}.glb\n  checkpoint, the gardens, all three river crossings, both trench ends, both\n  bunker flanks), with negative controls, and checks every wall lamp and\n  ivy patch has a wall behind it;\n  `tests/distance-check.mjs` — the horizon treelines face the level, sit\n  in the ground and leave the far village in sight:\n\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/world-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/route-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/character-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/ragdoll-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/distance-check.mjs\n\nURL switches for testing: `?debug` (frame stats), `?god`, `?fly` (free\ncamera; WASD, Q/E, Shift), `?at=x,z` (start elsewhere), `?go` (straight to\nthe briefing), `?test=<glb>` (drop a model in front of the free camera).\n\nDesign notes: `docs/2026-10-19-hedgerow-design.md`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e9c1ebcb-3878-4662-a001-d866fbdbd0e9","timestamp":"2026-10-21T07:12:29.930Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"gun reloads by itself after the last round. The enemy reloads too — five\nrounds for a Kar98k, 32 for an MP 40, a 75-round belt for the MG 42 — and\nducks while he does. The dead fall as ragdolls, pushed by the shot or thrown\nby the blast that killed them, and drop their rifles.\n\n## How it is built\n\n* `js/` — three.js r185 (the site's vendored copy), plain ES modules, no build.\n  * `main.js` boot, menus, frame loop · `levelBuild.js` level data → world ·\n    `levels/saint-clair.js` the mission (ground, props, enemies, objectives)\n  * `terrain.js` heightfield + splat material · `world.js` colliders, rays,\n    walking · `vegetation.js` instanced trees and ground cover with LOD\n  * `player.js`, `camera.js`, `character.js` (rig, split upper/lower body\n    animation), `ragdoll.js` (Verlet bodies driving the bones), `combat.js`\n    (hit volumes, grenades, charges, dropped magazines and rifles), `ai.js`\n    (perception, cover, MG nests, sniper, reloads), `mission.js`\n  * `distance.js` the countryside beyond the level: a terrain ring of fields\n    and woods to ~1 km with thousands of far-LOD trees, copses on the far\n    hills, rings of layered treeline cards on the horizon (150–350 m, facing\n    the level, open towards the far buildings) and the next village\n  * `materials.js` palette-keyed wet materials · `sky.js`, `weather.js`\n    (rain, splashes, lightning), `lights.js` (pooled point lights),\n    `effects.js` (particles), `atmosphere.js` (halos, mist, decals),\n    `post.js` + `bloom.js`, `audio.js` (procedural)\n* `assets/models/*.glb` — built by the Blender scripts in `tools/blender/`;\n  see `assets/models/MODELS.md` (pipeline, sizes, build commands),\n  `tools/blender/notes/` (every node) and `docs/models-brief*.md`:\n\n      /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender --background --factory-startup \\\n          --python fun/hedgerow/tools/blender/build_<set>.py\n      python3 -I fun/hedgerow/tools/fix_card_alpha.py fun/hedgerow/assets/models/{village,military,nature}.glb\n  checkpoint, the gardens, all three river crossings, both trench ends, both\n  bunker flanks), with negative controls, and checks every wall lamp and\n  ivy patch has a wall behind it;\n  `tests/distance-check.mjs` — the horizon treelines face the level, sit\n  in the ground and leave the far village in sight:\n\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/world-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/route-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/character-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/ragdoll-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/distance-check.mjs\n\nURL switches for testing: `?debug` (frame stats), `?god`, `?fly` (free\ncamera; WASD, Q/E, Shift), `?at=x,z` (start elsewhere), `?go` (straight to\nthe briefing), `?test=<glb>` (drop a model in front of the free camera).\n\nDesign notes: `docs/2026-10-19-hedgerow-design.md`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"924d5d5c-ca77-49d9-b20e-a90c62de5ba1","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow","branch":"hedgerow-poc","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":11,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"498b79f2-4ae6-4d8b-9755-5d48507abcd7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
