{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","id":"d17f7131-7351-4c51-88ec-864516e8107d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T07:13:03.582Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"ed0e1399c52579f98399aee39a809d021b3d830650734020ac7ed8991ce69af2","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"539f0440-613e-45d0-adab-dd472b88c69c","keep":862,"tail":["37ba236672b967d074f81b6c3d047cb0d6e1ccfdcd34757f700932775164f3d3","98b05aa82e8144a6a880e6974bdf23d53fac2d87260918ed5998f4de6e079eb5","07671479ca61734d81c3abce7722bc484d2583dbe5b764e79380c17707ad0df4"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",864,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"12b4d45255acc74ba6e15d6d4837145f8ea316585bf11e327f2d3b2438ec3912"}
{"parentUuid":"ae5842de-0035-4d74-a3f4-2c3e92cf8cb0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEy5nisXQoBWr4bSs7YT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The font, centered menus and games-page parts are done. The performance work is half in: the engine changes are written and all six tests pass, but the two low-detail model sets are still building in the background. Nothing is committed or pushed yet.\n\n**Font**\n- Every piece of text is now set in typewriter type: Courier Prime for the menus, HUD, briefing and settings, and Special Elite for the HEDGEROW wordmark and screen headings.\n- Both are free licensed fonts (OFL and Apache 2.0). I downloaded them from Google Fonts into the game's own `assets/fonts/` folder with their licence files, the same way the other games ship theirs. That's three files, 11–53 KB each.\n\n**Centered menus**\n- The pause, death, mission-complete, controls and settings panels now center their headings, text and buttons; before, headings and text were left-aligned.\n- The briefing paragraphs, the key list and the settings rows stay left-aligned inside centered blocks, so long text still reads well.\n- I checked every screen in the browser.\n\n**Performance**\nI measured before changing anything. At 1024×768 on your M1 Max a frame took 7.5–10.5 ms of GPU time. Most of that was geometry rather than pixels: halving the resolution saved only 0–4 ms.\n\n- **Enemies:** soldiers out of view are no longer drawn. Before, every enemy within 220 m was drawn even behind the camera. Their animation is also only updated five times a second while out of view. Draw calls at the start went from about 550 to 354.\n- **Resolution:** it now adjusts automatically, down to 60 % if frames run long and back up when there's headroom. That's the main help for weaker GPUs and high-density screens.\n- **Distant soldiers:** in-view enemies still cost about 1.8 ms. Each is the full 29k-triangle model even at 100 m. A ~5–6k-triangle low-detail version is building in the background, and the game is already set up to switch to it beyond 30 m.\n- **Mid-distance trees:** in the forest the full trees within 52 m cost about 2 ms. Thinned versions for 22–52 m are building, and the game is set up to use them too.\n\nA new test, `lod-check`, covers both detail switches, and I confirmed it fails when the tree switch is broken.\n\n**Games page**\nHedgerow now has a card at the end of the list on the Fun page and in the \"Play in your browser\" section of the home page, written like the others.\n\nYou stopped the test server partway through my measurements, so I've stayed out of the browser since. The two detail switches are covered only by the headless test.\n\n**Next steps**\nWhen the two builds finish I'll verify the new models and rerun the tests. Then I'll commit, rebase onto the current `main` and push to `main`. `main` has 8 new commits since this branch started. They touch only other parts of the home page, so the rebase should apply cleanly."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":885,"cache_read_input_tokens":623251,"output_tokens":951,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":885,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":951,"cache_read_input_tokens":623251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":885,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":885},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"32295f1e-a1ec-4c2f-a4e4-8f02b2135dc6","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgEy5nBsAAb3HNWQnhsev","requestRef":"d17f7131-7351-4c51-88ec-864