{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"c6f09148468ca244f38591238cbe0f288d866e515c4648b845e803fa6feed61b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"All four tests pass with the dressing fixes, including the new wall-mount check. Updating the model notes for village v3 now."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HZWaMJdQFwMy2KVLTbknLM","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"advance":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BiDV7ZbJpRMJMQPGzJJLDh","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/assets/models/MODELS.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"30a378ab31a2d725945dedee16e6bb92f48a5ec6b6acf93e7458173ccef5c480","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZWaMJdQFwMy2KVLTbknLM","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan updated: step 4 of 4 is in progress."}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BiDV7ZbJpRMJMQPGzJJLDh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Hedgerow models\n2\t\n3\tEvery GLB here is built by the committed Blender scripts in\n4\t`fun/hedgerow/tools/blender/`. Do not edit the GLBs by hand: change the\n5\tscripts and rebuild. The builds are deterministic (fixed seeds) and run in\n6\theadless Blender 5.3 on the CPU (Cycles bakes, no GPU needed).\n7\t\n8\t| file | built by | contents | size |\n9\t|---|---|---|---|\n10\t| `village.glb` | `build_village.py` | 42 nodes: 7 houses, barn, two ruins, church, walls, fences, bridge, street furniture, rubble, graves, ivy | 18.8 MB |\n11\t| `military.glb` | `build_military.py` | 42 nodes: sandbags, MG nest, bunker, trench pieces, wire, vehicles and wrecks, Flak 38, PaK 40, crates, signs, camouflage net | 12.3 MB |\n12\t| `nature.glb` | `build_nature.py` | 37 nodes: spruce, fir, Scots pine, oak, beech, birch (+ far LODs), hedgerows, bushes, ground cover, rocks, logs | 9.5 MB |\n13\t| `soldier.glb` | `build_soldier.py` | the rig (20 bones), US and German outfits, 16 animation clips | 4.6 MB |\n14\t| `weapons.glb` | `build_soldier.py` | M1 Garand, Thompson, Kar98k, MP 40, MG 42, two grenades | 1.9 MB |\n15\t\n16\t    /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender --background --factory-startup \\\n17\t        --python fun/hedgerow/tools/blender/build_<set>.py [-- node ... | flags]\n18\t    python3 -I fun/hedgerow/tools/fix_card_alpha.py fun/hedgerow/assets/models/{village,military,nature}.glb\n19\t\n20\tRun `fix_card_alpha.py` after building any set with alpha cards (nature,\n21\tmilitary, village): it fills the colour under the transparent texels and the\n22\tpale anti-aliased fringe of the foliage atlases from the opaque leaves, so the\n23\tmipmaps do not wash grass and leaves out at a distance. It is idempotent.\n24\t\n25\tEach set's notes (`tools/blender/notes/<set>.md`, written by the builds) list\n26\tevery node with its size, triangles, texture sizes, colliders and anchors.\n27\t`docs/models-brief.md` is the contract with the game (names, origins, front\n28\t= -Y in Blender = +Z in three.js, colliders and anchors in the node extras),\n29\t`docs/models-brief-v2.md` the realism pass.\n30\t\n31\t## How a model is made\n32\t\n33\t1. Geometry from bmesh primitives and lofts in the build script, each part\n34\t   given a **palette key** material (`kit.PALETTE`).\n35\t2. `bake.bake_model()` unwraps an atlas, bakes ambient occlusion (with a\n36\t   ground plane) and an edge mask, swaps every palette key for its\n37\t   procedural surface from `surfaces.py` (rubble limestone with mortar,\n38\t   plaster with stains and fallen patches, barrel tiles with lichen, slate,\n39\t   planks, peeling paint, chipped and rusted paint on steel, blued steel,\n40\t   board-formed concrete, hessian, wool, leather, skin, bark, granite...)\n41\t   plus shared weathering (occlusion, cavity dirt, splash at the base, rain\n42\t   streaks, moss, worn edges), then bakes base colour, roughness, metallic,\n43\t   emission and a tangent-space normal (bevelled edges + bump).\n44\t3. One material per node; WebP textures inside the GLB\n45\t   (`EXT_texture_webp`, which three.js r185's `GLTFLoader` reads).\n46\t4. Foliage, ivy and the camouflage net are alpha cards (glTF alphaMode\n47\t   MASK) on atlases rendered in Blender from modelled leaves, needles and\n48\t   blades; the game draws them double-sided with the alpha test, lit from\n49\t   the card normals, swaying in the wind.\n50\t\n51\tThe game replaces nothing in a baked material; it only adds the rain\n52\t(darker porous surfaces, glossier everything, water film and ripples on\n53\tupward faces) in `js/materials.js`.\n54\t\n55\tReview renders go to `tools/blender/previews/<set>/` (hundreds of MB, not\n56\tcommitted).\n57\t"}]}}
