{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"22c00dc22598fcbb1b8f9582b9f4267baa23c0372a3961d965fbacc6bea3464d","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pyv9cJszBdxhsLsRvkKPMf","type":"tool_result","content":"# Soldier set — notes\n\nBuilt by `tools/blender/build_soldier.py` (helpers in `soldier_parts.py`); this file is\nregenerated by every full build. All positions below are in **glTF / three.js space** (Y up,\nthe soldier faces **+Z**, his left is **+X**) unless marked Blender.\n\n    /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender --background --factory-startup \\\n        --python fun/hedgerow/tools/blender/build_soldier.py [-- soldier|weapons] [nopreview]\n\n## soldier.glb (4712 KB)\n\n| node | what | tris | material (baked) | textures | size x × y × z (m, Blender, rest) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `allied` | skinned mesh, child of `rig` | 21738 | `allied` | base 2048², normal 1024², mr 2048² | 1.25 × 0.51 × 1.78 |\n| `axis` | skinned mesh, child of `rig` | 22362 | `axis` | base 2048², normal 1024², mr 2048² | 1.25 × 0.48 × 1.77 |\n| `rig` | armature root node (identity) | | | | |\n| `socket_weapon` | empty, child of joint `hand_r` | | | | |\n| `socket_weapon_l` | empty, child of joint `hand_l` (extra, for the throw) | | | | |\n\nTriangles per part — allied: head 3890, neck 224, hands 1424, sleeves 2656, jacket 3252, collar 520, trousers 2688, leggings 1340, boots 1184, helmet 1276, webbing 3284.\nAxis: head 3890, neck 224, hands 1424, sleeves 2568, tunic 3896, collar 512, trousers 2560, boots 2596, helmet 1496, kit 3196.\nBoth meshes: stature 1.745 m (skull), helmet top ~1.77–1.78 m; ~21.7k / 22.4k tris (a little over the\nbrief's ~15–20k: the head, fingers and kit detail); ≤ 4 influences per vertex (3 used), weights\nnormalised. **v2**: each outfit is modelled from palette materials (wool, cotton drill, webbing, leather,\npainted steel, skin, …), then baked with `bake.bake_model` in the rest pose *before* skinning into ONE\nmaterial named after the mesh (`allied`, `axis`): base colour 2048², packed metallic-roughness 2048²,\ntangent-space normal 1024², WebP in the GLB. The bake carries the occlusion, stubble, lips, iris and\npupil, the cotton net over the M1 helmet, wear at the edges and mud splashed low on the legs; the\nvertex colour `Color` is flat white (kept for the shader contract). Before packing, the UV islands of\nthe face (×2.6), eyes (×3.2), hair (×1.4) and hands (×1.6) are scaled up so the face holds its detail.\nExtra palette keys registered at runtime by `soldier_parts.register_surfaces()` (no shared file edited):\n`skin` → skin with stubble/lips/cheeks, `eye`, `helmet_net`, `walnut`, `brass`, `bakelite`.\n\nGeometry (v2): sculpted head with eyeballs in almond lids, brow ridge, nose with wings, lips, chin,\nears with a helix rim, cropped hair cap; four fingers and a thumb closed round a bar (Ø39 mm right,\nØ47 mm left = the fore-end); uniforms with folds as geometry at the elbows (compression rolls), knees\n(back), waist (bloused above the belt), under the arms and down the skirt; seams, cuffs, collars.\nUS: M41 jacket with laid collar and lapels, wool shirt in the V, buttons, slash-pocket welts, cuff tabs,\nepaulettes; wool trousers bloused over M1938 leggings with hooks and crossing laces and an instep\nstrap; service shoes with soles and heels; M1 helmet with rolled rim, net (baked), liner and suspension\nband, bales, buckled webbing chin strap; M1923 belt with ten pockets and lift-the-dot snaps, first-aid\npouch, M1936 suspenders with buckles, M1928 haversack (flap, straps, buckles) with the M1943 e-tool and\nthe bayonet in its scabbard, canteen in its cover with snapped flaps. DE: M40 tunic with four pleated\npockets, scalloped flaps and buttons, stand collar with Litzen bars, shoulder boards; trousers bloused\ninto jackboots wrinkled at the ankle, hobnailed soles and heel irons; M40 Stahlhelm with rolled edge,\nsplit rivets, vent lugs, leather liner band, chin strap and buckle; belt and buckle with roundel,\nY-straps with D-rings, two three-cell pouches with strapped flaps and studs, bread bag, canteen with\ncup, fluted gas-mask canister with lid and rings, e-tool carrier and bayonet in its frog.\n\n### Bones (rest pose)\n\nEvery bone: local **+Y runs along the bone** to its child (Blender convention, kept by the exporter:\na child whose head sits on its parent's tail has rest translation `(0, parent_length, 0)`). For `root`, `hips`, `spine`,\n`chest`, `neck`, `head`, the arms and the legs the local **+Z points to the character's front** at rest\n(three +Z) and **X = Y × Z**; for the feet +Z points up. So for `spine`/`chest` the local X axis is the\nhorizontal towards the character's left (three +X) and **a positive rotation about local X bends forward /\npitches the rifle down**; aim pitch up = negative angle about local X. (Legs point down, so their X\nis three −X: + about X swings the leg back / bends the knee.)\n\n| bone | parent | head (glTF) | length | local X axis (glTF, rest) |\n5:the soldier faces **+Z**, his left is **+X**) unless marked Blender.\n14:| `allied` | skinned mesh, child of `rig` | 21738 | `allied` | base 2048², normal 1024², mr 2048² | 1.25 × 0.51 × 1.78 |\n15:| `axis` | skinned mesh, child of `rig` | 22362 | `axis` | base 2048², normal 1024², mr 2048² | 1.25 × 0.48 × 1.77 |\n20:Triangles per part — allied: head 3890, neck 224, hands 1424, sleeves 2656, jacket 3252, collar 520, trousers 2688, leggings 1340, boots 1184, helmet 1276, webbing 3284.\n21:Axis: head 3890, neck 224, hands 1424, sleeves 2568, tunic 3896, collar 512, trousers 2560, boots 2596, helmet 1496, kit 3196.\n23:brief's ~15–20k: the head, fingers and kit detail); ≤ 4 influences per vertex (3 used), weights\n25:painted steel, skin, …), then baked with `bake.bake_model` in the rest pose *before* skinning into ONE\n28:pupil, the cotton net over the M1 helmet, wear at the edges and mud splashed low on the legs; the\n30:the face (×2.6), eyes (×3.2), hair (×1.4) and hands (×1.6) are scaled up so the face holds its detail.\n31:Extra palette keys registered at runtime by `soldier_parts.register_surfaces()` (no shared file edited):\n32:`skin` → skin with stubble/lips/cheeks, `eye`, `helmet_net`, `walnut`, `brass`, `bakelite`.\n34:Geometry (v2): sculpted head with eyeballs in almond lids, brow ridge, nose with wings, lips, chin,\n53:a child whose head sits on its parent's tail has rest translation `(0, parent_length, 0)`). For `root`, `hips`, `spine`,\n54:`chest`, `neck`, `head`, the arms and the legs the local **+Z points to the character's front** at rest\n60:| bone | parent | head (glTF) | length | local X axis (glTF, rest) |\n67:| `head` | `neck` | (0.000, 1.555, -0.015) | 0.190 | (1.00, -0.00, 0.00) |\n134:| `death_fwd` | 40 | 1.333 |  | 0.51–1.74 | 0.26–0.93 | shot from the front: knees buckle, falls on the back (ends lying face up, head towards +Y Blender = -Z three) |\n135:| `death_back` | 40 | 1.333 |  | 0.44–1.74 | 0.16–0.96 | shot from behind: drops to the knees, falls face down (head towards -Y Blender = +Z three) |\n139:  barrel direction Blender (0.000, -1.000, 0.003) = glTF (0, 0, +1) — level, straight ahead.\n140:  The aiming (right) eye is within 1.2 cm of the sight line; the butt\n154:256²): blued steel worn bright at the edges, oiled walnut with grain and hand wear, leather slings with\n201:| `reload_smg` | `mag_out` | 17 | magazine clear of the well |\n210:* `grenade_us`: fuze up (+Y glTF), spoon on +X. `grenade_de`: head towards −Y Blender (+Z glTF), origin\n212:* Before the bake the Mk 2 body is `metal_olive`, the stick grenade head `metal_gray`; stocks `walnut`,\n217:* v3: the face/eye/hand texel boost now uses bake.py's new `scale_islands` hook (`soldier_parts.island_scaler`); nothing in bake.py is patched any more.\n219:* `export(objs, path, animations=True)` works for skins + actions; the soldier uses its own `export_scene.gltf` call only to turn on `export_optimize_animation_size` (+ `keep_anim_armature`).","is_error":false}]}}
