{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"b8d23dca158adb8a26e1bfff58c791506804b0179c8d4c398c0480d4341e86d9","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The cracks come from a Voronoi edge net and thin noise ridges, both drawn near-black at sub-pixel width (~8mm vs 1–2cm texture resolution), which causes the bake to break them into dashes. I'll check if the village build can bake just a single house so I can test fixes without a full 40-minute run.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S2QhTGeLdJWT1SeDQ2A1eY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow && grep -n \"sys.argv\\|def main\\|only\\|nopreview\\|preview\" tools/blender/build_village.py | head -30; grep -n -i \"texel\\|tpm\\|2560\" tools/blender/notes/village.md | head -10","description":"Check the village build's arguments and texel density"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"5a3c22a15560126eea0da05c9c6a787a30e9b2023381f4ba113c3b5c29648d45","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S2QhTGeLdJWT1SeDQ2A1eY","type":"tool_result","content":"4:        --python fun/hedgerow/tools/blender/build_village.py [-- [node ...] [--no-preview] [--dev]]\n6:No node names: build everything, export the GLB, render every preview and\n8:(it is cheap, ~2 s) but only preview the named nodes ('overview' is a name\n9:too). `--dev`: build only the named nodes and skip the export (iteration).\n10:`--no-preview`: skip the deliverable previews.\n557:    (enterable: colliders on the walls only), a hay loft and hay inside.\"\"\"\n2083:# Registry, previews, export\n2154:def preview_node(obj, name, size=768, samples=12):\n2155:    \"\"\"768 px previews: front 3/4, back 3/4, and a close-up from 2 m.\"\"\"\n2158:        kit.preview([obj], os.path.join(PREV, f'{name}{suffix}.png'), size=size, samples=samples, elevation=el, azimuth=az)\n2195:    kit.preview([obj] + made, path, size=512, samples=16, elevation=35, azimuth=-30)\n2219:def main():\n2224:    do_prev = '--no-preview' not in flags\n2248:        sc.cycles.use_denoising = True            # review renders only (bakes are done)\n2257:                preview_node(objs[n], n)\n2286:                    kit.preview([objs[n]], os.path.join(tmp, f'nrm_{n}_{suffix}.png'), size=384, samples=8, elevation=el, azimuth=az)\n38:  * Street houses a, b, c, e, f, g: base colour 2560, normal 1280,\n45:  * The street houses took 125–426 s each to bake at 2560 px.\n254:* **Texel density:**\n255:  * The street houses are baked at 2560 px.\n258:  * Street-facing (-Y) islands get about 30 % more texels; roofs and\n265:| house_a | rubble walls, ashlar dressings, proud stones, sill and eave stains, sagging shutters, two extra tile courses on the front slope, more missing and slipped tiles, mossy north slope, sooty stacks, 2560 px |\n266:| house_b | render, shell hole in the left wall, sill and eave stains, mossy north slate, dirty glass, 2560 px |\n267:| house_c | render, stains, more slipped tiles at the front eave, mossy north slope, 2560 px (the roof shell hole is unchanged) |\n268:| house_d | rubble walls, proud stones, mossy north thatch, worn steps, 140 tpm |\n269:| house_e | render, shell hole in the right wall (ground floor), stains on all four walls, 2560 px |","is_error":false}]}}
