{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"6533b5409ca8e18ad32f9e9cb9dc8f430f862b312a339680d3b0c6f93229aa0f","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018m92Ra9p3tUdmsGyuejSG3","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ae51200f68617c8f0","summary":"Resume soldier v4 after the network error","message":"You stopped on a network (API) error mid-task; please continue the soldier v4 pass from where you left off. Your Blender build is still running: pid 39481 (`build_soldier.py`, no args), started about 2 h 52 min ago at ~800 % CPU. Check its log/output before starting anything new; don't start a second soldier build while it runs. Note: I am iterating on the village plaster in a separate headless Blender process at the same time, so bakes will be slower than usual. Also: I edited tools/blender/bake.py to add an opt-in `samples_channels=1` parameter to bake_model (default unchanged, so your bakes are identical). Everything else in your brief stands: verify the GLB, run the five node checks, render and inspect face close-ups (base and each shape key) and the clip previews, update notes/soldier.md, and report back."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
