{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"a555547d10ab83b71f1e52a9c464bebf652903243533e0f50c4f07db577b2dd3","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plaster cracks are fixed up close, but there are still too many. A second version is test-baking now, and nothing has gone into the game yet.\n\n**Why they looked drawn on:**\n- **Too thin:** each crack was a line about 8 mm wide, but one texture pixel on a house covers about 1 cm. The bake also used one sample per pixel, so the lines broke into dashes.\n- **Too regular:** the lines came from a cell pattern, so they formed a net of near-black polygons across whole walls.\n\n**Results so far:**\n- **First version:** cracks about 1.5 cm wide with soft edges, dark grey-brown instead of black, a faint dirt halo, grime washing down below them and a few chipped edges. Close up they're continuous and no longer dashed. From a few metres away there were still too many, and closed cell shapes still gave the pattern away.\n- **Second version (baking now):**\n  - Fewer cracks, broken into open branching runs, about a fifth of each wall.\n  - They continue round the house corners.\n  - They cost about a third as much to bake.\n  - The colour bake uses 2 samples per texture pixel. The shared bake setting this uses is opt-in, so the other model sets still bake exactly as before.\n\n**Timing:** that one-house test bake took 1.9 hours instead of the usual 2–7 minutes. The soldier rebuild was using about 8 CPU cores at the same time, and the first crack version was heavier than it needed to be. Once the second test looks right I'll rebake the whole village. Expect that to take well over an hour while the soldier build is still running.\n\n**Soldier faces and bodies:** the background agent stopped on a network error partway through. Its Blender build kept running, and I've resumed the agent so it can finish, check the result and report. I'll wire the new faces into the game when it lands; the engine side is already done and tested.\n\nNothing is committed."}]}}
