{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"2cc5bea5fd9f51b63a94ebeebf36b80a463d401601f8179fa19aa91cdf8b43e8","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The new plaster recipe works in the test bakes of two houses, and the full village rebake has just started. The soldier faces and bodies are also rebuilt and in place. I haven't seen either in the game yet, and nothing is committed.\n\n**Plaster cracks** (house_b's side wall at 2 m and from the alley):\n- **Fewer and longer:** a handful of irregular cracks that fade out at their ends, plus a cluster round the shell hole. Most of the wall is clean.\n- **No longer dashed:** each crack is now 1.6–2.6 cm wide with soft edges, about two texture pixels. The village's colour bake also uses 2 samples per pixel now.\n- **Not black:** dark grey-brown, with a faint dirt halo and grime washed down below each crack.\n- **Panelling stripes gone:** the fine vertical stripes came from the shared rain-streak weathering. Rendered walls now get only a trace of it and keep their own broader stains.\n- **Not fixed:** house_e's side wall has a faint dotted rectangle that none of the recipe changes touched. Its shape points to a texture seam left by the shell-hole cut.\n\nA house now bakes in about 50 s. The 1.9-hour test earlier was the soldier build competing for the CPU.\n\n**Soldiers** (soldier.glb is now 6.6 MB, about 28–29k triangles per uniform):\n- **Faces:** matte skin with stubble and pores, real eyes (iris, lids, glossy cornea), proper ears, a thicker neck, and eyebrows built from hair strands.\n- **Chin straps:** the German one sits on the face; the US ones buckle up over the helmet rim.\n- **Bodies:** proper shoulders, arms and legs, hands with knuckles and nails, twill cloth with sweat stains, and better bends at shoulders, elbows and knees.\n- **Variety:** three face shapes (broad, gaunt, older). The game already gives each enemy a random blend of them, and a test covers that.\n- **Unchanged:** the rig, all 17 animations, the reload timing and the weapons file. The aiming eye stays within 1.2 cm of the rifle sights.\n\nThe faces still read somewhat CG: the lower face is long, the lips are a thin slit and the three face shapes differ only subtly. Fixing that takes another long soldier bake, so I'm holding it until the village rebuild finishes.\n\nWhen the village build finishes I'll verify the file and check that every node, collider and anchor matches the version before. Then I'll run the five tests and update the notes."}]}}
