{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"eb0b5287a005b28f5f64300cb0d8f8da31ca52be7869d89de6952a13d0ba94b4","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KpDhwuK2uswoyfrx9Uctgy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='tools/blender/notes/village.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"* **Render.** `plaster` and `plaster_dirty` now bake as lime render:\n  * blotches and trowel texture;\n  * crazing and long cracks;\n  * blown patches with a broken rim showing the rubble;\n  * vertical run-off stains;\n  * algae and splash at the foot.\n\"\"\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,\"\"\"* **Render.** `plaster` and `plaster_dirty` now bake as lime render:\n  * blotches and trowel texture;\n  * a few long cracks (see below);\n  * blown patches with a broken rim showing the rubble;\n  * broad vertical run-off stains;\n  * algae and splash at the foot.\n* **Render cracks (reworked).** The first v3 cracks were Voronoi cell edges\n  about 8 mm wide in near-black, baked at one sample per texel (~1 cm):\n  they came out as dashed black lines in a polygon net, as if drawn on.\n  Now (`_crack_dist`, `_crack_mask` in `village_parts.py`):\n  * a domain-warped 2D Voronoi net in (x + y, z), so cracks meander, run\n    on round the corners and cost a third of a 3D net;\n  * kept on about a quarter of each wall and broken now and then into long\n    open runs, so no closed cells show;\n  * 1.6-2.6 cm across with soft edges (never under a texel), fading out at\n    their ends, dark grey-brown; a faint dirt halo, grime washed down below\n    (the crack field sampled 8 and 24 cm higher) and chips of render lost\n    along the edges; a shallow groove in the normal map;\n  * render has its own weathering profile (`render`): the shared fine rain\n    streaks made regular vertical stripes on a smooth wall, so only a trace\n    of them is left;\n  * the village bakes its colour/roughness/metal channels at 2 samples per\n    texel (`bake_model(..., samples_channels=2)`).\n  * Review shots: `--detail` renders house_b's cracked side wall and house_e\n    (`det_house_b_*.png`, `det_house_e_*.png` in `$TMPDIR`).\n  * Known: house_e's right wall shows a faint dotted rectangle near the\n    shell hole that does not come from the recipe (a seam from the breach\n    cut, by its shape); not chased.\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='assets/models/MODELS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"graves, ivy | 20.5 MB |\",\"graves, ivy | 20.3 MB |\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"20.3 MB\" assets/models/MODELS.md | head -2; sed -n 84,100p README.md","description":"Document the crack rework and update the village size"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"01af560a5f93ea1d44e357422179c90e805a31eb2ddd7fc8d953fb1c8f356d2e","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KpDhwuK2uswoyfrx9Uctgy","type":"tool_result","content":"10:| `village.glb` | `build_village.py` | 42 nodes: 7 houses (three with shell holes through a wall), barn, two ruins, church, walls, fences, bridge, street furniture, rubble, graves, ivy | 20.3 MB |\n  bake), `surfaces.py` (procedural surfaces).\n* `assets/textures/*.webp` — tileable detail textures from\n  `python3 fun/hedgerow/tools/textures.py`.\n* `tests/world-check.mjs` — collision world unit checks;\n  `tests/character-check.mjs` — the aim pitch stays put under held poses\n  (three's mixer skips unchanged bones), reload clip timing and the hand prop;\n  `tests/ragdoll-check.mjs` — a shot soldier falls, is pushed by the shot,\n  keeps his limbs' length and comes to rest;\n  `tests/route-check.mjs` — rebuilds the level's collision world from the\n  real GLB colliders and walks every route (main road, both flanks of the\n  checkpoint, the gardens, all three river crossings, both trench ends, both\n  bunker flanks), with negative controls, and checks every wall lamp and\n  ivy patch has a wall behind it;\n  `tests/distance-check.mjs` — the horizon treelines face the level, sit\n  in the ground and leave the far village in sight:\n\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/world-check.mjs\n[This command modified 2 files you've previously read: tools/blender/notes/village.md, assets/models/MODELS.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]}}
