{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"6dfc96338c3066faf2af09903705e7e1308618680e2007c7cfe3293da814e2a9","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The current face shapes only shift the head by a few millimeters, far too subtle compared to the 1–2 cm variation in real faces—these won't read at game distance. I'll send the agent a second-pass brief with concrete targets to fix this.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FRRMUa28wqiHjnLLvHmXRE","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ae51200f68617c8f0","summary":"Soldier face pass 2: proportions, lips, jaw, shapes","message":"Second soldier face pass, requested by the user: \"shorter lower face, fuller lips, a wider jaw, and more distinct face shapes\". The CPU is free now (my village rebuild is finished, nothing else is baking). Same files, constraints and budgets as before (rig/bones/clips/reload_events/sockets/node names/one skinned mesh + one material per outfit unchanged; soldier.glb ≤ 7 MB; ≤ 32k tris per outfit; deterministic; no commits, no browser, no server; don't touch kit.py/bake.py/surfaces.py/JS/other sets; restore weapons.glb byte-identical if the full build re-exports it).\n\nWhat I see in your v4 previews (axis_rest_face_34, allied_rest_face_front, axis_rest_face_older_face_34): better skin and eyes, but the head reads long and narrow (\"horse face\"): the lower third (nose base to chin) is too long, the jaw is narrow, the lips are a thin slit, and the three shapes barely differ. I measured the morph targets in the GLB: face_broad moves vertices max 8.9 mm (mean 2.9 mm over 1957 verts), face_gaunt max 5.1 mm (mean 1.7), face_older max 4.9 mm (mean 1.8). That cannot read at game distance (3–15 m).\n\nTargets for the base head:\n1. Facial thirds about equal for a young adult male: hairline–brow ≈ brow–nose base ≈ nose base–chin ≈ 6.0–6.5 cm. Shorten the lower third by ~10–12 % by raising the chin/jaw line, not by moving the eyes, nose root or skull (the aiming eye must stay within ~1.5 cm of the sight line as now — re-measure and report).\n2. Fuller lips: upper vermilion ~7–8 mm tall, lower ~9–10 mm, mouth ~5 cm wide, defined cupid's bow and philtrum columns, lips closed with a soft parting line and slightly darker, slightly depressed corners. Not a slit.\n3. Wider jaw: bigonial (jaw-angle) width ~11.5–12 cm against a zygomatic (cheekbone) width ~13.5–14 cm, a clear jaw angle with masseter mass, a chin ~4 cm wide. Neck and collars must still fit (re-check the German stand collar and both chin straps).\n4. Eye sockets: you noted they read dark and tired — lighten the occlusion there a little so the eyes read.\n\nTargets for the shape keys (same names and index order: 0 face_broad, 1 face_gaunt, 2 face_older), each clearly a different man at weight 1 and still readable at 0.5:\n- face_broad: heavier, wider face — jaw and cheeks out 10–15 mm per side, fuller cheeks and a thicker neck under the jaw, broader nose (+15–20 % nostril width), heavier brow, shorter-looking chin. Max displacement ~15–20 mm, mean over the moved region ≥ 5 mm.\n- face_gaunt: lean, hollow — cheeks sunk 8–12 mm below the cheekbones, cheekbones and jaw angle prominent, temples hollow, narrower chin, longer thinner nose, thinner lips. Similar magnitudes.\n- face_older (35–45 years): deeper nasolabial folds and marionette lines, jowls dropping 5–8 mm at the jaw line, heavier upper lids and lower-lid bags, a softer jaw line, thinner lips, a slightly longer nose tip. Must be geometric (one shared texture).\n- Blends: broad+older and gaunt+older must look sane. The engine picks per enemy: build = U(-1,1); face_broad = max(0, build), face_gaunt = max(0, -build), face_older = U·U·0.9.\n- The morphs must not move the eye apexes (sight line), must keep the German chin strap on the skin (it follows the morph now — keep that), and the US straps clear.\n\nDeliverables: rebuild soldier.glb; verify by script as before (and report the new max/mean displacement per morph target, and the GLB size — if over 7 MB, tell me what you traded); run the five node checks; render face previews (front/34/side) for base and each key at 1.0, plus one line-up image per outfit of 6 soldiers side by side at 34 view with seeded random blends from the engine's distribution above (print the weights used), and the usual clip previews; look at them yourself and iterate before reporting; update the v4 section of notes/soldier.md (call it v4.1) and the MODELS.md soldier row if the size changes. Report what changed, the measurements, the previews to open, and anything that still doesn't land."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
