{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"dc752d0d88407943f10d79c43143e5a19c9aaa47459df1b8c1dd6ae280deab4a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The light specks at the boot tops only appear on the German low-detail mesh, which matters since German soldiers are the enemies visible from 30m+. I'm resuming the soldier agent to fix just that seam, asking it to rework the existing low-detail mesh rather than rerun the hour-long bake.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TBV6RMyHQiEy32LESFSaTv","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ae51200f68617c8f0","summary":"Fix the axis LOD boot-top seam specks","message":"You dropped on a network error after the LOD build finished. I've checked the result: soldier.glb is 7.22 MB, and I accept that size (don't trim it). I verified by script that only `allied_lod` / `axis_lod` were added (5791 / 5799 tris, skin 0, materials shared, no targets) and everything else matches the committed file. I restored weapons.glb from git (your build had re-exported it; it is byte-identical to the commit again — keep it that way).\n\nOne defect to fix, in your axis_lod_compare.png: the German LOD shows light/white specks at the boot tops and on the shins (columns 2 and 4, rows 1–2), at 30 m too. It looks like the collapse pulled UVs across a seam there (the boot/trouser boundary), so some triangles sample empty atlas space. allied_lod looks clean, but check it the same way.\n\nPlease fix it with the fastest safe path, ideally regenerating just the two LOD meshes from the existing soldier.glb (e.g. import the GLB, re-decimate the full mesh with UV-seam/boundary vertices protected, transfer weights, re-export with the same images/materials), instead of a full re-bake — if you do re-export the whole file, make sure the full meshes, morph targets, rig, clips, reload_events and textures are identical to now and weapons.glb stays untouched (restore it from git with `git checkout -- fun/hedgerow/assets/models/weapons.glb` if your build re-exports it). Then: verify by script as before, re-render the two *_lod_compare.png previews and look at the boot tops, run the six node checks (there is a new tests/lod-check.mjs), update the v4.2 notes, and report back. No commits, no browser, no server."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
