{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"db65976175581ce7c24dfae6957905ed067afe663ce134efb80ccdb2961ed8ff","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The low-detail soldiers are built, with one defect being fixed: light specks at the boot tops of the German soldier, the enemy you'll see most. The tree build is still running, and nothing is committed or pushed.\n\n- **Soldiers:** each uniform has a low-detail version of about 5.8k triangles, against 29k for the full model. It reuses the same skeleton, materials and textures. I compared the file with the committed one: only the two new meshes were added, and the rig, animations, reload timing and face shapes are unchanged.\n- **File size:** soldier.glb is now 7.2 MB, a little over the 7 MB cap I'd set. The low-detail meshes add about 0.9 MB, and trimming it isn't worth another long rebuild.\n- **Boot-top specks:** in the 30 m comparison renders, the US version matches the full model, but the German one has these specks. The agent dropped on a network error just after its build, so I've resumed it to fix only that. I asked it to rebuild only the low-detail meshes from the existing file, if possible, rather than redo the hour-long bake.\n- **Weapons file:** the soldier build had re-exported `weapons.glb`, so I restored it from git and it's identical to the committed version again.\n\nWhen both agents report, I'll verify the files and run the tests. Then I'll commit, rebase onto `main` and push to `main`."}]}}
