e v4.2 section of `notes/soldier.md` now describes the normal transfer, the UV check, and that `character.js` switches at 30 m (back at 26 m). The soldier row in `MODELS.md` now lists the LODs and 7.3 MB. Nothing is committed.\n\n**Still not quite right**\n- The file grew about 66 KB because the transferred normals split more vertices; that's the size over 7 MB.\n- Up close the LODs are visibly faceted and the small buttons and studs are gone. That's by design for a mesh used only beyond 26 m."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":10,"turnIndex":39},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
