{"parentUuid":"a023b1f8-44f1-4a89-8467-395c124cb288","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF7ifrq763wGpwmtQrZB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your disk filled up completely while the tree models were building. Both build attempts failed with \"no space left on device\", and free space fell to 213 MB of 926 GiB. It has since recovered to 22 GiB, so I've rerun the build. I didn't delete anything to get there. Nothing is committed or pushed yet.\n\n- **What happened:** the tree agent saw free space drop by about 500 MB in five minutes during its second attempt, more than its build writes. Something else on the machine, possibly swap, is taking space. If the disk is close to full on your end, it's worth freeing some.\n- **The build now running:** it's the same tree build again, plus renders comparing each full tree with its middle-distance version. I kept a copy of the current tree file, so a failed or truncated build can be undone.\n- **One thing to check:** the big oak's middle-distance version came out with about 80 % of the original leaf area, against 93 % in the agent's previous tuning. I'll judge it from the comparison renders.\n- **Fallback:** if this build fails or the trees don't look right, I'll push everything else on its own. That covers the font, the centered menus, the enemy culling, the dynamic resolution, the soldier low-detail models and the games-page cards. The unfinished tree work would stay in a separate local commit to finish later. The game uses the middle tree versions only if they exist, so it's safe either way.\n\nOnce the build reports, I'll check the renders, run the six tests, then commit, rebase onto `main` and push."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":721,"cache_read_input_tokens":669389,"output_tokens":484,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_to