{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"34d4edb1bc50eb42b97f2026d41dbf4b20b9e0259e85fdfee30c06327d3ee998","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found the issue: a 0.55m sandbag wall at z 217 that the grid incorrectly let soldiers step onto (0.7m allowance) when they can only climb 0.45m. I've fixed this so raised surfaces like sandbags and decks only connect within 0.45m, while natural ground slopes keep the original 0.7m allowance.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0115KauMXgYAtpFHUXCKMnvo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='js/nav.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nreps=[\n(\"\"\"export function createNav(world, { minX, maxX, minZ, maxZ }, { cell = 2, radius = 0.4, step = 0.7 } = {}) {\"\"\",\n \"\"\"export function createNav(world, { minX, maxX, minZ, maxZ }, { cell = 2, radius = 0.4, slope = 0.7, step = 0.45 } = {}) {\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  // raised footing counts only where it joins the ground: bridges stay,\n  // the tops of walls, roofs and tree trunks (islands) are dropped\n  {\n    const seen = new Uint8Array(n);\n    const raised = (k) => h[k] === h[k] && h[k] > th[k] + 0.45;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  // footing on something (a deck, a step): the climb onto it is limited to\n  // what a soldier can step up (`step`); over the terrain only the slope\n  // between cells (`slope`)\n  const raised = new Uint8Array(n);\n  for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) raised[k] = h[k] === h[k] && h[k] > th[k] + 0.2 ? 1 : 0;\n  const linkH = (a, b) => Math.abs(h[a] - h[b]) <= (raised[a] || raised[b] ? step : slope);\n  // raised footing counts only where it joins the ground: bridges stay,\n  // the tops of walls, roofs and tree trunks (islands) are dropped\n  {\n    const seen = new Uint8Array(n);\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"          if (!(h[o] === h[o]) || Math.abs(h[o] - h[k]) > step) continue;\n          if (!raised(o)) { joins = true; continue; }\"\"\",\n\"\"\"          if (!(h[o] === h[o]) || !linkH(o, k)) continue;\n          if (!raised[o]) { joins = true; continue; }\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"      if (seen[k0] || !raised(k0)) continue;\"\"\", \"\"\"      if (seen[k0] || !raised[k0]) continue;\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  const link = (a, b) => walkable(a) && walkable(b) && Math.abs(h[a] - h[b]) <= step;\"\"\",\n \"\"\"  const link = (a, b) => walkable(a) && walkable(b) && linkH(a, b);\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode --check js/nav.js && node $TMPDIR/navprobe.mjs && node tests/ai-check.mjs 2>&1 | tail -14","description":"Limit climbs onto raised surfaces and rerun the checks","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
