{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"2d5a0f2af95b581de46c687679a8c6fede9ec6107abc7ae17d94b4de91def23b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"In the square the lamp posts get a subtle glow at 30 m and the scene stays crisp. Round 1 is done. Running the tests and committing it."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014wFv6QHSnP7AdnTkfqukab","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow && for f in js/*.js js/levels/*.js; do node --check $f || echo \"SYNTAX $f\"; done; for t in character-check lod-check distance-check; do node tests/$t.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1; done && cd .. && cd .. && git add fun/hedgerow && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: light in the rain\n\nA volumetric pass, first in the effect chain so it reads the scene's\ndepth: for up to eight of the strongest lights near the camera (lamps,\nfires, muzzle flashes, explosions) the light scattered towards the eye\nalong each view ray, in closed form (the airlight integral of an\ninverse-square point light, up to the surface the pixel shows), with a\nforward-leaning phase function and rain curtains drifting with the wind.\nLamps glow in the wet air, a fire lights the haze and its smoke, and\nanything in front of a light cuts its glow. ~0.4 ms GPU at 1024x768 on\nan M1 Max; on the high and medium presets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Check and commit the volumetric light round","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
