opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"41e7b17b-22d5-419f-b589-46ff15a64527","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ca86ac74-b393-4b38-8e69-5ddecc3498f5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011uh3Y4x6ug6tN7EnM2FsNy","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"1c01a0c8-9872-49a5-bda8-42d900f3a2df","timestamp":"2026-10-21T10:41:32.403Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/README.md","oldString":"fires, halos in the wet air, low mist, bullet holes and scorch marks, distant\nartillery flashes and burning farms beyond the hedges.","newString":"fires, halos in the wet air, low mist, bullet holes and scorch marks, distant\nartillery flashes and burning farms beyond the hedges. Lamps and fires cast\nsoft shadows and their light hangs in the rain between you and them, corners\nand the ground under things darken, and the frame is finished like film —\ncontrast, sharpening, grain in the shadows — going soft behind whatever you\naim at.","originalFile":"# Hedgerow\n\nA third-person Second World War shooter for the browser — realistic-looking,\narcade to play. You are one soldier pushing through hand-built missions; this\nproof of concept has the first one:\n\n**Mission 1 — Saint-Clair, at dusk.** Normandy, July 1944, evening, rain.\nUp a sunken lane between hedgerows, through the checkpoint into the village,\nup the main street to the church square (sniper in the tower), over the\nriver (bridge under a machine gun, a ford downstream, a fallen tree\nupstream), through the forest's foxholes and trench line, past a concrete\nbunker, to the flak gun in the clearing — blow it up — and on to the rally\npoint.\n\nEvery defended point has more than one way past it: the orchard or the ditch\nround the checkpoint, the back gardens or the ruined house along the street,\nthree river crossings, the ends of the trench, the flanks of the bunker.\n\nThe look is built for realism at dusk in the rain: every model carries baked\nPBR textures (stone courses and mortar, peeling paint, rusted and chipped\nsteel, hessian, wool, bark and moss, with occlusion, grime and rain streaks\nbaked in), foliage is alpha cards rendered from modelled leaves, and the\nrenderer adds wet reflective ground with puddle ripples, rain lit by lamps and\nfires, halos in the wet air, low mist, bullet holes and scorch marks, distant\nartillery flashes and burning farms beyond the hedges.\n\n## Controls\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Mouse | look and aim |\n| W A S D | move |\n| Shift | sprint |\n| C / Ctrl | crouch (toggle) |\n| Space | vault low cover / jump |\n| Left / right button | fire / aim down the sights |\n| R | reload |\n| 1 / 2 / wheel | M1 Garand / Thompson |\n| G | grenade (hold to cook) |\n| E | use (set the charge) |\n| Q | switch shoulder |\n| Esc | pause |\n\nHealth comes back when you stay out of fire. Dying returns you to the last\ncheckpoint; the enemies you killed stay dead.\n\nThe Germans are not statues. Patrols walk their beats and stop to look\nround. A shot or a grenade heard from a distance sends one or two of a\ngroup to look while the rest get into cover facing the sound. Break contact\nand they split up: some search where you were last seen and look round the\ncorners nearby, and if you were on the move some run ahead along your way,\ncrouch behind cover and wait for you to walk into their sights. Afterwards\nthey go back to their posts, warier for a while. When one of them kills you\nthe camera turns to him and follows him — usually as he walks over to make\nsure.\n\nReloading is a real motion: the empty Thompson magazine drops to the ground\nand a fresh one comes up in the left hand; the Garand's empty clip flies out\nwith its ping on the last shot. R reloads, an empty trigger reloads, and the\ngun reloads by itself after the last round. The enemy reloads too — five\nrounds for a Kar98k, 32 for an MP 40, a 75-round belt for the MG 42 — and\nducks while he does. The dead fall as ragdolls, pushed by the shot or thrown\nby the blast that killed them, and drop their rifles.\n\n## How it is built\n\n* `js/` — three.js r185 (the site's vendored copy), plain ES modules, no build.\n  * `main.js` boot, menus, frame loop with dynamic resolution (holds ~60 fps\n    by scaling the render down to 60 % on slow GPUs and dense screens, and\n    back up when there is headroom) · `levelBuild.js` level data → world ·\n    `levels/saint-clair.js` the mission (ground, props, enemies, objectives)\n  * `terrain.js` heightfield + splat material · `world.js` colliders, rays,\n    walking · `vegetation.js` instanced trees and ground cover in up to\n    three tiers: full model, a thinned `_mid` beyond ~22 m when the nature\n    set has one, the `_lod` impostor beyond the quality's near range\n  * `player.js`, `camera.js`, `character.js` (rig, split upper/lower body\n    animation, the outfit's low-detail `_lod` mesh beyond 30 m), `ragdoll.js` (Verlet bodies driving the bones), `combat.js`\n    (hit volumes, grenades, charges, dropped magazines and rifles), `ai.js`\n    (perception, cover, MG nests, sniper, reloads; patrols; sounds looked\n    into; a lost player searched for where he was seen and ambushed along\n    his way; the killer checks the body; soldiers out of view are not drawn\n    and are posed five times a second), `nav.js` (the 2 m walk grid and A*\n    paths round houses, walls and the river), `mission.js`\n  * `distance.js` the countryside beyond the level: a terrain ring of fields\n    and woods to ~1 km with thousands of far-LOD trees, copses on the far\n    hills, rings of layered treeline cards on the horizon (150–350 m, facing\n    the level, open towards the far buildings) and the next village\n  * `materials.js` palette-keyed wet materials · `sky.js`, `weather.js`\n    (rain, splashes, lightning), `lights.js` (pooled point lights),\n    `effects.js` (particles), `atmosphere.js` (halos, mist, decals),\n    `post.js` + `bloom.js`, `audio.js` (procedural)\n* `assets/models/*.glb` — built by the Blender scripts in `tools/blender/`;\n  see `assets/models/MODELS.md` (pipeline, sizes, build commands),\n  `tools/blender/notes/` (every node) and `docs/models-brief*.md`:\n\n      /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender --background --factory-startup \\\n          --python fun/hedgerow/tools/blender/build_<set>.py\n      python3 -I fun/hedgerow/tools/fix_card_alpha.py fun/hedgerow/assets/models/{village,military,nature}.glb\n\n  for `village`, `military`, `nature` and `soldier` (soldier + weapons).\n  Shared: `kit.py` (modelling helpers, palette, export), `bake.py` (the PBR\n  bake), `surfaces.py` (procedural surfaces).\n* `assets/textures/*.webp` — tileable detail textures from\n  `python3 fun/hedgerow/tools/textures.py`.\n* `tests/world-check.mjs` — collision world unit checks;\n  `tests/character-check.mjs` — the aim pitch stays put under held poses\n  (three's mixer skips unchanged bones), reload clip timing and the hand prop,\n  per-soldier face blends (each enemy mixes the rig's `face_broad`,\n  `face_gaunt` and `face_older` shape keys);\n  `tests/ragdoll-check.mjs` — a shot soldier falls, is pushed by the shot,\n  keeps his limbs' length and comes to rest;\n  `tests/route-check.mjs` — rebuilds the level's collision world from the\n  real GLB colliders and walks every route (main road, both flanks of the\n  checkpoint, the gardens, all three river crossings, both trench ends, both\n  bunker flanks), with negative controls, and checks every wall lamp and\n  ivy patch has a wall behind it;\n  `tests/distance-check.mjs` — the horizon treelines face the level, sit\n  in the ground and leave the far village in sight;\n  `tests/lod-check.mjs` — soldiers switch to low detail at a distance\n  (with a gap so they don't flicker), trees sort into full, mid and far;\n  `tests/ai-check.mjs` — on the real level: every patrol route walkable, a\n  patrol walks it, a distant shot is looked into, lost contact means a\n  search and an ambush (hidden, facing his way, springing from cover), the\n  killer walks to the body, the death camera follows him:\n\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/world-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/route-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/character-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/ragdoll-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/distance-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/lod-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/ai-check.mjs\n\nURL switches for testing: `?debug` (frame stats), `?god`, `?fly` (free\ncamera; WASD, Q/E, Shift), `?at=x,z` (start elsewhere), `?go` (straight to\nthe briefing), `?test=<glb>` (drop a model in front of the free camera).\n\nType: everything is set on the typewriter — Courier Prime (OFL) for the\ninterface and Special Elite (Apache 2.0) for the wordmark and headings,\nself-hosted in `assets/fonts/` with their licences.\n\nDesign notes: `docs/2026-10-19-hedgerow-design.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":22,"oldLines":7,"newStart":22,"newLines":11,"lines":[" baked in), foliage is alpha cards rendered from modelled leaves, and the"," renderer adds wet reflective ground with puddle ripples, rain lit by lamps and"," fires, halos in the wet air, low mist, bullet holes and scorch marks, distant","-artillery flashes and burning farms beyond the hedges.","+artillery flashes and burning farms beyond the hedges. Lamps and fires cast","+soft shadows and their light hangs in the rain between you and them, corners","+and the ground under things darken, and the frame is finished like film —","+contrast, sharpening, grain in the shadows — going soft behind whatever you","+aim at."," "," ## Controls"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"eccdc0a9-197a-4ea7-8603-14b4450d56fc","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow","branch":"hedgerow-poc","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"41e7b17b-22d5-419f-b589-46ff15a64527","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"1817677f-3965-41d1-a519-d41660d48364","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ca86ac74-b393-4b38-8e69-5ddecc3498f5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hn6Qrh7fiMX2o4TrvRJSYF","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"dffb56ac-fa66-4b4f-ae35-a08e378cd2ba","timestamp":"2026-10-21T10:41:32.444Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/README.md","oldString":"    `effects.js` (particles), `atmosphere.js` (halos, mist, decals),\n    `post.js` + `bloom.js`, `audio.js` (procedural)","newString":"    `effects.js` (particles), `atmosphere.js` (halos, mist, decals),\n    `audio.js` (procedural)\n  * the effects chain (`renderer.setEffects`, in order): `ssao.js` ambient\n    occlusion at half resolution · `volumetric.js` lays the occlusion on\n    and adds the light scattered in the rain by up to eight lamps, fires and\n    flashes (the closed-form airlight integral, cut by the depth) · `dof.js`\n    focus on what is under the crosshair while aiming · `bloom.js` ·\n    `post.js` the grade (sharpening, contrast, colour, vignette, grain, the\n    hurt state); the high and medium qualities run all of it, low only the\n    grade","originalFile":"# Hedgerow\n\nA third-person Second World War shooter for the browser — realistic-looking,\narcade to play. You are one soldier pushing through hand-built missions; this\nproof of concept has the first one:\n\n**Mission 1 — Saint-Clair, at dusk.** Normandy, July 1944, evening, rain.\nUp a sunken lane between hedgerows, through the checkpoint into the village,\nup the main street to the church square (sniper in the tower), over the\nriver (bridge under a machine gun, a ford downstream, a fallen tree\nupstream), through the forest's foxholes and trench line, past a concrete\nbunker, to the flak gun in the clearing — blow it up — and on to the rally\npoint.\n\nEvery defended point has more than one way past it: the orchard or the ditch\nround the checkpoint, the back gardens or the ruined house along the street,\nthree river crossings, the ends of the trench, the flanks of the bunker.\n\nThe look is built for realism at dusk in the rain: every model carries baked\nPBR textures (stone courses and mortar, peeling paint, rusted and chipped\nsteel, hessian, wool, bark and moss, with occlusion, grime and rain streaks\nbaked in), foliage is alpha cards rendered from modelled leaves, and the\nrenderer adds wet reflective ground with puddle ripples, rain lit by lamps and\nfires, halos in the wet air, low mist, bullet holes and scorch marks, distant\nartillery flashes and burning farms beyond the hedges. Lamps and fires cast\nsoft shadows and their light hangs in the rain between you and them, corners\nand the ground under things darken, and the frame is finished like film —\ncontrast, sharpening, grain in the shadows — going soft behind whatever you\naim at.\n\n## Controls\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Mouse | look and aim |\n| W A S D | move |\n| Shift | sprint |\n| C / Ctrl | crouch (toggle) |\n| Space | vault low cover / jump |\n| Left / right button | fire / aim down the sights |\n| R | reload |\n| 1 / 2 / wheel | M1 Garand / Thompson |\n| G | grenade (hold to cook) |\n| E | use (set the charge) |\n| Q | switch shoulder |\n| Esc | pause |\n\nHealth comes back when you stay out of fire. Dying returns you to the last\ncheckpoint; the enemies you killed stay dead.\n\nThe Germans are not statues. Patrols walk their beats and stop to look\nround. A shot or a grenade heard from a distance sends one or two of a\ngroup to look while the rest get into cover facing the sound. Break contact\nand they split up: some search where you were last seen and look round the\ncorners nearby, and if you were on the move some run ahead along your way,\ncrouch behind cover and wait for you to walk into their sights. Afterwards\nthey go back to their posts, warier for a while. When one of them kills you\nthe camera turns to him and follows him — usually as he walks over to make\nsure.\n\nReloading is a real motion: the empty Thompson magazine drops to the ground\nand a fresh one comes up in the left hand; the Garand's empty clip flies out\nwith its ping on the last shot. R reloads, an empty trigger reloads, and the\ngun reloads by itself after the last round. The enemy reloads too — five\nrounds for a Kar98k, 32 for an MP 40, a 75-round belt for the MG 42 — and\nducks while he does. The dead fall as ragdolls, pushed by the shot or thrown\nby the blast that killed them, and drop their rifles.\n\n## How it is built\n\n* `js/` — three.js r185 (the site's vendored copy), plain ES modules, no build.\n  * `main.js` boot, menus, frame loop with dynamic resolution (holds ~60 fps\n    by scaling the render down to 60 % on slow GPUs and dense screens, and\n    back up when there is headroom) · `levelBuild.js` level data → world ·\n    `levels/saint-clair.js` the mission (ground, props, enemies, objectives)\n  * `terrain.js` heightfield + splat material · `world.js` colliders, rays,\n    walking · `vegetation.js` instanced trees and ground cover in up to\n    three tiers: full model, a thinned `_mid` beyond ~22 m when the nature\n    set has one, the `_lod` impostor beyond the quality's near range\n  * `player.js`, `camera.js`, `character.js` (rig, split upper/lower body\n    animation, the outfit's low-detail `_lod` mesh beyond 30 m), `ragdoll.js` (Verlet bodies driving the bones), `combat.js`\n    (hit volumes, grenades, charges, dropped magazines and rifles), `ai.js`\n    (perception, cover, MG nests, sniper, reloads; patrols; sounds looked\n    into; a lost player searched for where he was seen and ambushed along\n    his way; the killer checks the body; soldiers out of view are not drawn\n    and are posed five times a second), `nav.js` (the 2 m walk grid and A*\n    paths round houses, walls and the river), `mission.js`\n  * `distance.js` the countryside beyond the level: a terrain ring of fields\n    and woods to ~1 km with thousands of far-LOD trees, copses on the far\n    hills, rings of layered treeline cards on the horizon (150–350 m, facing\n    the level, open towards the far buildings) and the next village\n  * `materials.js` palette-keyed wet materials · `sky.js`, `weather.js`\n    (rain, splashes, lightning), `lights.js` (pooled point lights),\n    `effects.js` (particles), `atmosphere.js` (halos, mist, decals),\n    `post.js` + `bloom.js`, `audio.js` (procedural)\n* `assets/models/*.glb` — built by the Blender scripts in `tools/blender/`;\n  see `assets/models/MODELS.md` (pipeline, sizes, build commands),\n  `tools/blender/notes/` (every node) and `docs/models-brief*.md`:\n\n      /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender --background --factory-startup \\\n          --python fun/hedgerow/tools/blender/build_<set>.py\n      python3 -I fun/hedgerow/tools/fix_card_alpha.py fun/hedgerow/assets/models/{village,military,nature}.glb\n\n  for `village`, `military`, `nature` and `soldier` (soldier + weapons).\n  Shared: `kit.py` (modelling helpers, palette, export), `bake.py` (the PBR\n  bake), `surfaces.py` (procedural surfaces).\n* `assets/textures/*.webp` — tileable detail textures from\n  `python3 fun/hedgerow/tools/textures.py`.\n* `tests/world-check.mjs` — collision world unit checks;\n  `tests/character-check.mjs` — the aim pitch stays put under held poses\n  (three's mixer skips unchanged bones), reload clip timing and the hand prop,\n  per-soldier face blends (each enemy mixes the rig's `face_broad`,\n  `face_gaunt` and `face_older` shape keys);\n  `tests/ragdoll-check.mjs` — a shot soldier falls, is pushed by the shot,\n  keeps his limbs' length and comes to rest;\n  `tests/route-check.mjs` — rebuilds the level's collision world from the\n  real GLB colliders and walks every route (main road, both flanks of the\n  checkpoint, the gardens, all three river crossings, both trench ends, both\n  bunker flanks), with negative controls, and checks every wall lamp and\n  ivy patch has a wall behind it;\n  `tests/distance-check.mjs` — the horizon treelines face the level, sit\n  in the ground and leave the far village in sight;\n  `tests/lod-check.mjs` — soldiers switch to low detail at a distance\n  (with a gap so they don't flicker), trees sort into full, mid and far;\n  `tests/ai-check.mjs` — on the real level: every patrol route walkable, a\n  patrol walks it, a distant shot is looked into, lost contact means a\n  search and an ambush (hidden, facing his way, springing from cover), the\n  killer walks to the body, the death camera follows him:\n\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/world-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/route-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/character-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/ragdoll-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/distance-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/lod-check.mjs\n      node fun/hedgerow/tests/ai-check.mjs\n\nURL switches for testing: `?debug` (frame stats), `?god`, `?fly` (free\ncamera; WASD, Q/E, Shift), `?at=x,z` (start elsewhere), `?go` (straight to\nthe briefing), `?test=<glb>` (drop a model in front of the free camera).\n\nType: everything is set on the typewriter — Courier Prime (OFL) for the\ninterface and Special Elite (Apache 2.0) for the wordmark and headings,\nself-hosted in `assets/fonts/` with their licences.\n\nDesign notes: `docs/2026-10-19-hedgerow-design.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":92,"oldLines":7,"newStart":92,"newLines":15,"lines":["   * `materials.js` palette-keyed wet materials · `sky.js`, `weather.js`","     (rain, splashes, lightning), `lights.js` (pooled point lights),","     `effects.js` (particles), `atmosphere.js` (halos, mist, decals),","-    `post.js` + `bloom.js`, `audio.js` (procedural)","+    `audio.js` (procedural)","+  * the effects chain (`renderer.setEffects`, in order): `ssao.js` ambient","+    occlusion at half resolution · `volumetric.js` lays the occlusion on","+    and adds the light scattered in the rain by up to eight lamps, fires and","+    flashes (the closed-form airlight integral, cut by the depth) · `dof.js`","+    focus on what is under the crosshair while aiming · `bloom.js` ·","+    `post.js` the grade (sharpening, contrast, colour, vignette, grain, the","+    hurt state); the high and medium qualities run all of it, low only the","+    grade"," * `assets/models/*.glb` — built by the Blender scripts in `tools/blender/`;","   see `assets/models/MODELS.md` (pipeline, sizes, build commands),","   `tools/blender/notes/` (every node) and `docs/models-brief*.md`:"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"eccdc0a9-197a-4ea7-8603-14b4450d56fc","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow","branch":"hedgerow-poc","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1817677f-3965-41d1-a519-d41660d48364","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"871