{"parentUuid":"67e59896-89e0-44e7-b2a8-5c6c3c49e991","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFJvpPQnT1AHNfnAh6bu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WuM48KxusQjjyuZEHKShqA","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js","old_string":"   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js onto the scene first: the\n   half-resolution occlusion brought up with a depth-aware 3 x 3 filter\n   (so it does not bleed across edges), sparing bright pixels — lamps,\n   fires and lit windows are not darkened by what is near them. */","new_string":"   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js and the reflections of\n   ssr.js onto the scene first: both half-resolution, brought up with one\n   depth-aware 3 x 3 filter (so they do not bleed across edges). The\n   occlusion spares bright pixels — lamps, fires and lit windows are not\n   darkened by what is near them — and so do the reflections, which take\n   the place of what the material reflected (the sky) in proportion to how\n   mirror-like the scene pass says the pixel is (its alpha). */"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4535,"cache_read_input_tokens":199526,"output_tokens":3281,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":217},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4535,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3281,"cache_read_input_tokens":199526,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4535},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WuM48KxusQjjyuZEHKShqA":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js","old_string":"   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js onto the scene first: the\n   half-resolution occlusion brought up with a depth-aware 3 x 3 filter\n   (so it does not bleed across edges), sparing bright pixels — lamps,\n   fires and lit windows are not darkened by what is near them. */","new_string":"   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js and the reflections of\n   ssr.js onto the scene first: both half-resolution, brought up with one\n   depth-aware 3 x 3 filter (so they do not bleed across edges). The\n   occlusion spares bright pixels — lamps, fires and lit windows are not\n   darkened by what is near them — and so do the reflections, which take\n   the place of what the material reflected (the sky) in proportion to how\n   mirror-like the scene pass says the pixel is (its alpha). */"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0fc81173-55a9-40a2-ad78-1a8caf7b8a80","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgFJvp44ze4FBrNhgnvSQ","requestRef":"c062596a-180e-476a-9de3-e2c13b90dec0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"76ddf700-5c84-4909-8bd0-01dfca0323b1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T11:33:24.588Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"76ddf700-5c84-4909-8bd0-01dfca0323b1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFJvpPQnT1AHNfnAh6bu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016bovY3JJ8cLb8ej6Q1YH5K","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js","old_string":"uniform sampler2D tAO;\nuniform vec2 uAOTexel;\nuniform float uAO;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\n\nfloat viewZ(vec2 uv) {\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, uv).x;\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(uv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  return v.z / v.w;\n}\nfloat occlusion(vec2 uv, float z0) {\n  float sum = 0.0, wsum = 0.0;\n  for (int j = -1; j <= 1; j++) for (int i = -1; i <= 1; i++) {\n    vec2 o = vec2(float(i), float(j)) * uAOTexel;\n    float w = (i == 0 && j == 0 ? 2.0 : 1.0) / (0.02 + abs(viewZ(uv + o) - z0));\n    sum += texture2D(tAO, uv + o).r * w;\n    wsum += w;\n  }\n  return sum / wsum;\n}","new_string":"uniform sampler2D tAO, tSSR;\nuniform vec2 uAOTexel;\nuniform float uAO, uSSR;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\n\nfloat viewZ(vec2 uv) {\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, uv).x;\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(uv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  return v.z / v.w;\n}\n// the half-resolution layers brought up to full size, weighted by depth likeness\nvoid layers(vec2 uv, float z0, bool refl, out float ao, out vec4 rf) {\n  float wsum = 0.0;\n  ao = 0.0; rf = vec4(0.0);\n  for (int j = -1; j <= 1; j++) for (int i = -1; i <= 1; i++) {\n    vec2 o = vec2(float(i), float(j)) * uAOTexel;\n    float w = (i == 0 && j == 0 ? 2.0 : 1.0) / (0.02 + abs(viewZ(uv + o) - z0));\n    ao += texture2D(tAO, uv + o).r * w;\n    if (refl) rf += texture2D(tSSR, uv + o) * w;\n    wsum += w;\n  }\n  ao /= wsum; rf /= wsum;\n}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4535,"ca