{"parentUuid":"0e518e4b-9dc1-4543-b053-149a31175f8e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFJvpPQnT1AHNfnAh6bu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KDtTQVsGvfm1kZP6YJD39z","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js","old_string":"    setAO(ssao, strength = 0.85) {\n      u.tAO.value = ssao ? ssao.texture : null;\n      u.uAOTexel.value = ssao ? ssao.uniforms.uTexel.value : u.uAOTexel.value;\n      u.uAO.value = ssao ? strength : 0;\n    },","new_string":"    setAO(ssao, strength = 0.85) {\n      u.tAO.value = ssao ? ssao.texture : null;\n      u.uAOTexel.value = ssao ? ssao.uniforms.uTexel.value : u.uAOTexel.value;\n      u.uAO.value = ssao ? strength : 0;\n    },\n    /* the reflections pass to lay on (ssr.js, at the occlusion's half\n       resolution: the upsample shares its texel), and how strongly */\n    setSSR(ssr, strength = 1) {\n      u.tSSR.value = ssr ? ssr.texture : null;\n      u.uSSR.value = ssr ? strength : 0;\n    },"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4535,"cache_read_input_tokens":199526,"output_tokens":3281,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":217},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4535,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3281,"cache_read_input_tokens":199526,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4535},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KDtTQVsGvfm1kZP6YJD39z":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js","old_string":"    setAO(ssao, strength = 0.85) {\n      u.tAO.value = ssao ? ssao.texture : null;\n      u.uAOTexel.value = ssao ? ssao.uniforms.uTexel.value : u.uAOTexel.value;\n      u.uAO.value = ssao ? strength : 0;\n    },","new_string":"    setAO(ssao, strength = 0.85) {\n      u.tAO.value = ssao ? ssao.texture : null;\n      u.uAOTexel.value = ssao ? ssao.uniforms.uTexel.value : u.uAOTexel.value;\n      u.uAO.value = ssao ? strength : 0;\n    },\n    /* the reflections pass to lay on (ssr.js, at the occlusion's half\n       resolution: the upsample shares its texel), and how strongly */\n    setSSR(ssr, strength = 1) {\n      u.tSSR.value = ssr ? ssr.texture : null;\n      u.uSSR.value = ssr ? strength : 0;\n    },"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0fc81173-55a9-40a2-ad78-1a8caf7b8a80","apiBlockIndex":6,"requestId":"req_011CgFJvp44ze4FBrNhgnvSQ","requestRef":"c062596a-180e-476a-9de3-e2c13b90dec0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"78e80aaf-19ee-4fa3-a95b-203c77641026","timestamp":"2026-10-21T11:33:41.554Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"76ddf700-5c84-4909-8bd0-01dfca0323b1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ca86ac74-b393-4b38-8e69-5ddecc3498f5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WuM48KxusQjjyuZEHKShqA","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"984ba427-2950-4cec-962e-593679fcc5d4","timestamp":"2026-10-21T11:33:41.876Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js","oldString":"   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js onto the scene first: the\n   half-resolution occlusion brought up with a depth-aware 3 x 3 filter\n   (so it does not bleed across edges), sparing bright pixels — lamps,\n   fires and lit windows are not darkened by what is near them. */","newString":"   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js and the reflections of\n   ssr.js onto the scene first: both half-resolution, brought up with one\n   depth-aware 3 x 3 filter (so they do not bleed across edges). The\n   occlusion spares bright pixels — lamps, fires and lit windows are not\n   darkened by what is near them — and so do the reflections, which take\n   the place of what the material reflected (the sky) in proportion to how\n   mirror-like the scene pass says the pixel is (its alpha). */","originalFile":"/* Hedgerow — light in the rain.\n\n   A pass for `renderer.setEffects`, first in the chain (it reads the\n   scene's depth): the glow that lamps, fires, muzzle flashes and\n   explosions put into the wet air between the camera and whatever each\n   pixel sees. For a point light in an even medium the light scattered\n   towards the eye along a view ray has a closed form (the \"airlight\"\n   integral): with the ray's closest approach to the light at distance h\n   and parameter t0, the inverse-square falloff integrates to\n       (atan((t1 - t0) / h) - atan((ta - t0) / h)) / h\n   over the stretch [ta, t1] of the ray inside the light's range, and that\n   stretch ends at the surface the pixel shows — so a wall in front of a\n   lamp hides the lamp's glow behind it, and a soldier walking past a fire\n   cuts a dark shape out of its haze. A forward-leaning phase function\n   makes lights ahead of the camera glow more than those behind it, and a\n   slow noise drifting with the wind breaks the haze into rain curtains.\n   Up to eight of the strongest lights near the camera (the light pool's\n   choice, lights.js) take part each frame.\n\n   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js onto the scene first: the\n   half-resolution occlusion brought up with a depth-aware 3 x 3 filter\n   (so it does not bleed across edges), sparing bright pixels — lamps,\n   fires and lit windows are not darkened by what is near them. */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\n\nconst MAX = 8;\n\nconst VERT = /* glsl */ `\nvarying vec2 vUv;\nvoid main() { vUv = uv; gl_Position = vec4(position.xy, 0.0, 1.0); }`;\n\nconst FRAG = /* glsl */ `\n#define MAX ${MAX}\nuniform sampler2D tSrc;\nuniform sampler2D tDepth;\nuniform mat4 uProjInv, uViewInv;\nuniform vec3 uCam;\nuniform vec3 uPos[MAX];\nuniform vec3 uCol[MAX];\nuniform float uRange[MAX];\nuniform int uCount;\nuniform float uDensity, uTime, uRain, uFar;\nuniform vec2 uWind;\nuniform sampler2D tAO;\nuniform vec2 uAOTexel;\nuniform float uAO;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\n\nfloat viewZ(vec2 uv) {\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, uv).x;\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(uv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  return v.z / v.w;\n}\nfloat occlusion(vec2 uv, float z0) {\n  float sum = 0.0, wsum = 0.0;\n  for (int j = -1; j <= 1; j++) for (int i = -1; i <= 1; i++) {\n    vec2 o = vec2(float(i), float(j)) * uAOTexel;\n    float w = (i == 0 && j == 0 ? 2.0 : 1.0) / (0.02 + abs(viewZ(uv + o) - z0));\n    sum += texture2D(tAO, uv + o).r * w;\n    wsum += w;\n  }\n  return sum / wsum;\n}\n\nfloat hash(vec3 p) { p = fract(p * 0.3183099 + 0.1); p *= 17.0; return fract(p.x * p.y * p.z * (p.x + p.y + p.z)); }\nfloat noise(vec3 x) {\n  vec3 i = floor(x), f = fract(x);\n  f = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f);\n  return mix(mix(mix(hash(i), hash(i + vec3(1, 0, 0)), f.x), mix(hash(i + vec3(0, 1, 0)), hash(i + vec3(1, 1, 0)), f.x), f.y),\n             mix(mix(hash(i + vec3(0, 0, 1)), hash(i + vec3(1, 0, 1)), f.x), mix(hash(i + vec3(0, 1, 1)), hash(i + vec3(1, 1, 1)), f.x), f.y), f.z);\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n  vec3 col = texture2D(tSrc, vUv).rgb;\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, vUv).x;\n  // the view ray and the distance to what this pixel shows\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(vUv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  v.xyz /= v.w;\n  float T = d >= 1.0 ? uFar : min(length(v.xyz), uFar);\n  if (uAO > 0.0 && d < 1.0) {\n    float ao = occlusion(vUv, v.z);\n    float lum = dot(col, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722));\n    col *= mix(1.0, ao, uAO * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.8, 5.0, lum)));\n  }\n  vec3 dir = normalize(mat3(uViewInv) * v.xyz);\n  vec3 add = vec3(0.0);\n  for (int i = 0; i < MAX; i++) {\n    if (i >= uCount) break;\n    vec3 L = uPos[i] - uCam;\n    float t0 = dot(L, dir);\n    float h2 = max(dot(L, L) - t0 * t0, 0.0);\n    float R = uRange[i];\n    if (h2 > R * R) continue;\n    // the stretch of the ray inside the light's range, cut by the surface\n    float w = sqrt(R * R - h2);\n    float ta = max(0.0, t0 - w), tb = min(T, t0 + w);\n    if (tb <= ta) continue;\n    float h = sqrt(h2) + 0.35;                 // a soft core: no singularity at the bulb\n    float I = (atan((tb - t0) / h) - atan((ta - t0) / h)) / h;\n    // fade towards the edge of the range like the light itself\n    float edge = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.55, 1.0, sqrt(h2) / R);\n    // forward scattering (Henyey-Greenstein, g = 0.45) seen from the closest point\n    float c = t0 / max(length(L), 1e-3);\n    float g = 0.45;\n    float phase = 0.0795775 * (1.0 - g * g) / pow(1.0 + g * g - 2.0 * g * c, 1.5);\n    // rain curtains drifting with the wind, round the closest point of approach\n    vec3 q = uCam + dir * clamp(t0, ta, tb);\n    float n = noise(vec3(q.x * 0.35 + uWind.x * uTime, q.y * 0.18 - uTime * 0.9, q.z * 0.35 + uWind.y * uTime));\n    add += uCol[i] * I * edge * phase * (0.55 + 0.9 * n);\n  }\n  col += add * uDensity * (0.6 + 0.4 * uRain);\n  gl_FragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);\n}`;\n\nexport function createVolumetric(camera) {\n  const geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n  geometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([-1, 3, 0, -1, -1, 0, 3, -1, 0], 3));\n  geometry.setAttribute('uv', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([0, 2, 0, 0, 2, 0], 2));\n  const material = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({\n    vertexShader: VERT, fragmentShader: FRAG,\n    uniforms: {\n      tSrc: { value: null }, tDepth: { value: null },\n      uProjInv: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() }, uViewInv: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() },\n      uCam: { value: new THREE.Vector3() },\n      uPos: { value: Array.from({ length: MAX }, () => new THREE.Vector3()) },\n      uCol: { value: Array.from({ length: MAX }, () => new THREE.Vector3()) },\n      uRange: { value: new Array(MAX).fill(1) },\n      uCount: { value: 0 },\n      uDensity: { value: 0.03 }, uTime: { value: 0 }, uRain: { value: 1 }, uFar: { value: 140 },\n      uWind: { value: new THREE.Vector2(0.5, 0.2) },\n      tAO: { value: null }, uAOTexel: { value: new THREE.Vector2(1, 1) }, uAO: { value: 0 },\n    },\n    depthTest: false, depthWrite: false, toneMapped: false,\n  });\n  const quad = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);\n  quad.frustumCulled = false;\n  const ortho = new THREE.OrthographicCamera(-1, 1, 1, -1, 0, 1);\n  const u = material.uniforms;\n\n  return {\n    enabled: true, needsSwap: true, uniforms: u,\n    /* this frame's lights: [{x, y, z, color, intensity, range}] */\n    setLights(list, time, rain = 1) {\n      const n = Math.min(MAX, list.length);\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        const l = list[i];\n        u.uPos.value[i].set(l.x, l.y, l.z);\n        u.uCol.value[i].set(l.color.r, l.color.g, l.color.b).multiplyScalar(l.intensity);\n        u.uRange.value[i] = l.range * 0.8;\n      }\n      u.uCount.value = n;\n      u.uTime.value = time;\n      u.uRain.value = rain;\n    },\n    /* the occlusion pass to apply (ssao.js), and how strongly (0: none) */\n    setAO(ssao, strength = 0.85) {\n      u.tAO.value = ssao ? ssao.texture : null;\n      u.uAOTexel.value = ssao ? ssao.uniforms.uTexel.value : u.uAOTexel.value;\n      u.uAO.value = ssao ? strength : 0;\n    },\n    render(renderer, writeBuffer, readBuffer) {\n      if (!readBuffer.depthTexture) { this.enabled = false; return; }\n      camera.updateMatrixWorld();\n      u.uProjInv.value.copy(camera.projectionMatrixInverse);\n      u.uViewInv.value.copy(camera.matrixWorld);\n      u.uCam.value.setFromMatrixPosition(camera.matrixWorld);\n      u.tSrc.value = readBuffer.texture;\n      u.tDepth.value = readBuffer.depthTexture;\n      renderer.setRenderTarget(writeBuffer);\n      renderer.render(quad, ortho);\n    },\n  };\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":10,"newStart":17,"newLines":13,"lines":["    Up to eight of the strongest lights near the camera (the light pool's","    choice, lights.js) take part each frame."," ","-   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js onto the scene first: the","-   half-resolution occlusion brought up with a depth-aware 3 x 3 filter","-   (so it does not bleed across edges), sparing bright pixels — lamps,","-   fires and lit windows are not darkened by what is near them. */","+   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js and the reflections of","+   ssr.js onto the scene first: both half-resolution, brought up with one","+   depth-aware 3 x 3 filter (so they do not bleed across edges). The","+   occlusion spares bright pixels — lamps, fires and lit windows are not","+   darkened by what is near them — and so do the reflections, which take","+   the place of what the material reflected (the sky) in proportion to how","+   mirror-like the scene pass says the pixel is (its alpha). */"," "," import * as THREE from 'three';"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0fc81173-55a9-40a2-ad78-1a8caf7b8a80","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow","branch":"hedgerow-poc","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"76ddf700-5c84-4909-8bd0-01dfca0323b1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"c3bddef3-6a16-4b91-8fa5-d9004372caa8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ca86ac74-b393-4b38-8e69-5ddecc3498f5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016bovY3JJ8cLb8ej6Q1YH5K","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"017e6601-f073-4168-af12-da0d15fe071f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T11:33:41.914Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js","oldString":"uniform sampler2D tAO;\nuniform vec2 uAOTexel;\nuniform float uAO;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\n\nfloat viewZ(vec2 uv) {\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, uv).x;\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(uv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  return v.z / v.w;\n}\nfloat occlusion(vec2 uv, float z0) {\n  float sum = 0.0, wsum = 0.0;\n  for (int j = -1; j <= 1; j++) for (int i = -1; i <= 1; i++) {\n    vec2 o = vec2(float(i), float(j)) * uAOTexel;\n    float w = (i == 0 && j == 0 ? 2.0 : 1.0) / (0.02 + abs(viewZ(uv + o) - z0));\n    sum += texture2D(tAO, uv + o).r * w;\n    wsum += w;\n  }\n  return sum / wsum;\n}","newString":"uniform sampler2D tAO, tSSR;\nuniform vec2 uAOTexel;\nuniform float uAO, uSSR;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\n\nfloat viewZ(vec2 uv) {\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, uv).x;\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(uv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  return v.z / v.w;\n}\n// the half-resolution layers brought up to full size, weighted by depth likeness\nvoid layers(vec2 uv, float z0, bool refl, out float ao, out vec4 rf) {\n  float wsum = 0.0;\n  ao = 0.0; rf = vec4(0.0);\n  for (int j = -1; j <= 1; j++) for (int i = -1; i <= 1; i++) {\n    vec2 o = vec2(float(i), float(j)) * uAOTexel;\n    float w = (i == 0 && j == 0 ? 2.0 : 1.0) / (0.02 + abs(viewZ(uv + o) - z0));\n    ao += texture2D(tAO, uv + o).r * w;\n    if (refl) rf += texture2D(tSSR, uv + o) * w;\n    wsum += w;\n  }\n  ao /= wsum; rf /= wsum;\n}","originalFile":"/* Hedgerow — light in the rain.\n\n   A pass for `renderer.setEffects`, first in the chain (it reads the\n   scene's depth): the glow that lamps, fires, muzzle flashes and\n   explosions put into the wet air between the camera and whatever each\n   pixel sees. For a point light in an even medium the light scattered\n   towards the eye along a view ray has a closed form (the \"airlight\"\n   integral): with the ray's closest approach to the light at distance h\n   and parameter t0, the inverse-square falloff integrates to\n       (atan((t1 - t0) / h) - atan((ta - t0) / h)) / h\n   over the stretch [ta, t1] of the ray inside the light's range, and that\n   stretch ends at the surface the pixel shows — so a wall in front of a\n   lamp hides the lamp's glow behind it, and a soldier walking past a fire\n   cuts a dark shape out of its haze. A forward-leaning phase function\n   makes lights ahead of the camera glow more than those behind it, and a\n   slow noise drifting with the wind breaks the haze into rain curtains.\n   Up to eight of the strongest lights near the camera (the light pool's\n   choice, lights.js) take part each frame.\n\n   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js and the reflections of\n   ssr.js onto the scene first: both half-resolution, brought up with one\n   depth-aware 3 x 3 filter (so they do not bleed across edges). The\n   occlusion spares bright pixels — lamps, fires and lit windows are not\n   darkened by what is near them — and so do the reflections, which take\n   the place of what the material reflected (the sky) in proportion to how\n   mirror-like the scene pass says the pixel is (its alpha). */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\n\nconst MAX = 8;\n\nconst VERT = /* glsl */ `\nvarying vec2 vUv;\nvoid main() { vUv = uv; gl_Position = vec4(position.xy, 0.0, 1.0); }`;\n\nconst FRAG = /* glsl */ `\n#define MAX ${MAX}\nuniform sampler2D tSrc;\nuniform sampler2D tDepth;\nuniform mat4 uProjInv, uViewInv;\nuniform vec3 uCam;\nuniform vec3 uPos[MAX];\nuniform vec3 uCol[MAX];\nuniform float uRange[MAX];\nuniform int uCount;\nuniform float uDensity, uTime, uRain, uFar;\nuniform vec2 uWind;\nuniform sampler2D tAO;\nuniform vec2 uAOTexel;\nuniform float uAO;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\n\nfloat viewZ(vec2 uv) {\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, uv).x;\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(uv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  return v.z / v.w;\n}\nfloat occlusion(vec2 uv, float z0) {\n  float sum = 0.0, wsum = 0.0;\n  for (int j = -1; j <= 1; j++) for (int i = -1; i <= 1; i++) {\n    vec2 o = vec2(float(i), float(j)) * uAOTexel;\n    float w = (i == 0 && j == 0 ? 2.0 : 1.0) / (0.02 + abs(viewZ(uv + o) - z0));\n    sum += texture2D(tAO, uv + o).r * w;\n    wsum += w;\n  }\n  return sum / wsum;\n}\n\nfloat hash(vec3 p) { p = fract(p * 0.3183099 + 0.1); p *= 17.0; return fract(p.x * p.y * p.z * (p.x + p.y + p.z)); }\nfloat noise(vec3 x) {\n  vec3 i = floor(x), f = fract(x);\n  f = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f);\n  return mix(mix(mix(hash(i), hash(i + vec3(1, 0, 0)), f.x), mix(hash(i + vec3(0, 1, 0)), hash(i + vec3(1, 1, 0)), f.x), f.y),\n             mix(mix(hash(i + vec3(0, 0, 1)), hash(i + vec3(1, 0, 1)), f.x), mix(hash(i + vec3(0, 1, 1)), hash(i + vec3(1, 1, 1)), f.x), f.y), f.z);\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n  vec3 col = texture2D(tSrc, vUv).rgb;\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, vUv).x;\n  // the view ray and the distance to what this pixel shows\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(vUv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  v.xyz /= v.w;\n  float T = d >= 1.0 ? uFar : min(length(v.xyz), uFar);\n  if (uAO > 0.0 && d < 1.0) {\n    float ao = occlusion(vUv, v.z);\n    float lum = dot(col, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722));\n    col *= mix(1.0, ao, uAO * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.8, 5.0, lum)));\n  }\n  vec3 dir = normalize(mat3(uViewInv) * v.xyz);\n  vec3 add = vec3(0.0);\n  for (int i = 0; i < MAX; i++) {\n    if (i >= uCount) break;\n    vec3 L = uPos[i] - uCam;\n    float t0 = dot(L, dir);\n    float h2 = max(dot(L, L) - t0 * t0, 0.0);\n    float R = uRange[i];\n    if (h2 > R * R) continue;\n    // the stretch of the ray inside the light's range, cut by the surface\n    float w = sqrt(R * R - h2);\n    float ta = max(0.0, t0 - w), tb = min(T, t0 + w);\n    if (tb <= ta) continue;\n    float h = sqrt(h2) + 0.35;                 // a soft core: no singularity at the bulb\n    float I = (atan((tb - t0) / h) - atan((ta - t0) / h)) / h;\n    // fade towards the edge of the range like the light itself\n    float edge = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.55, 1.0, sqrt(h2) / R);\n    // forward scattering (Henyey-Greenstein, g = 0.45) seen from the closest point\n    float c = t0 / max(length(L), 1e-3);\n    float g = 0.45;\n    float phase = 0.0795775 * (1.0 - g * g) / pow(1.0 + g * g - 2.0 * g * c, 1.5);\n    // rain curtains drifting with the wind, round the closest point of approach\n    vec3 q = uCam + dir * clamp(t0, ta, tb);\n    float n = noise(vec3(q.x * 0.35 + uWind.x * uTime, q.y * 0.18 - uTime * 0.9, q.z * 0.35 + uWind.y * uTime));\n    add += uCol[i] * I * edge * phase * (0.55 + 0.9 * n);\n  }\n  col += add * uDensity * (0.6 + 0.4 * uRain);\n  gl_FragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);\n}`;\n\nexport function createVolumetric(camera) {\n  const geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n  geometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([-1, 3, 0, -1, -1, 0, 3, -1, 0], 3));\n  geometry.setAttribute('uv', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([0, 2, 0, 0, 2, 0], 2));\n  const material = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({\n    vertexShader: VERT, fragmentShader: FRAG,\n    uniforms: {\n      tSrc: { value: null }, tDepth: { value: null },\n      uProjInv: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() }, uViewInv: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() },\n      uCam: { value: new THREE.Vector3() },\n      uPos: { value: Array.from({ length: MAX }, () => new THREE.Vector3()) },\n      uCol: { value: Array.from({ length: MAX }, () => new THREE.Vector3()) },\n      uRange: { value: new Array(MAX).fill(1) },\n      uCount: { value: 0 },\n      uDensity: { value: 0.03 }, uTime: { value: 0 }, uRain: { value: 1 }, uFar: { value: 140 },\n      uWind: { value: new THREE.Vector2(0.5, 0.2) },\n      tAO: { value: null }, uAOTexel: { value: new THREE.Vector2(1, 1) }, uAO: { value: 0 },\n    },\n    depthTest: false, depthWrite: false, toneMapped: false,\n  });\n  const quad = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);\n  quad.frustumCulled = false;\n  const ortho = new THREE.OrthographicCamera(-1, 1, 1, -1, 0, 1);\n  const u = material.uniforms;\n\n  return {\n    enabled: true, needsSwap: true, uniforms: u,\n    /* this frame's lights: [{x, y, z, color, intensity, range}] */\n    setLights(list, time, rain = 1) {\n      const n = Math.min(MAX, list.length);\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        const l = list[i];\n        u.uPos.value[i].set(l.x, l.y, l.z);\n        u.uCol.value[i].set(l.color.r, l.color.g, l.color.b).multiplyScalar(l.intensity);\n        u.uRange.value[i] = l.range * 0.8;\n      }\n      u.uCount.value = n;\n      u.uTime.value = time;\n      u.uRain.value = rain;\n    },\n    /* the occlusion pass to apply (ssao.js), and how strongly (0: none) */\n    setAO(ssao, strength = 0.85) {\n      u.tAO.value = ssao ? ssao.texture : null;\n      u.uAOTexel.value = ssao ? ssao.uniforms.uTexel.value : u.uAOTexel.value;\n      u.uAO.value = ssao ? strength : 0;\n    },\n    render(renderer, writeBuffer, readBuffer) {\n      if (!readBuffer.depthTexture) { this.enabled = false; return; }\n      camera.updateMatrixWorld();\n      u.uProjInv.value.copy(camera.projectionMatrixInverse);\n      u.uViewInv.value.copy(camera.matrixWorld);\n      u.uCam.value.setFromMatrixPosition(camera.matrixWorld);\n      u.tSrc.value = readBuffer.texture;\n      u.tDepth.value = readBuffer.depthTexture;\n      renderer.setRenderTarget(writeBuffer);\n      renderer.render(quad, ortho);\n    },\n  };\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":45,"oldLines":9,"newStart":45,"newLines":9,"lines":[" uniform int uCount;"," uniform float uDensity, uTime, uRain, uFar;"," uniform vec2 uWind;","-uniform sampler2D tAO;","+uniform sampler2D tAO, tSSR;"," uniform vec2 uAOTexel;","-uniform float uAO;","+uniform float uAO, uSSR;"," varying vec2 vUv;"," "," float viewZ(vec2 uv) {"]},{"oldStart":55,"oldLines":15,"newStart":55,"newLines":18,"lines":["   vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(uv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);","   return v.z / v.w;"," }","-float occlusion(vec2 uv, float z0) {","-  float sum = 0.0, wsum = 0.0;","+// the half-resolution layers brought up to full size, weighted by depth likeness","+void layers(vec2 uv, float z0, bool refl, out float ao, out vec4 rf) {","+  float wsum = 0.0;","+  ao = 0.0; rf = vec4(0.0);","   for (int j = -1; j <= 1; j++) for (int i = -1; i <= 1; i++) {","     vec2 o = vec2(float(i), float(j)) * uAOTexel;","     float w = (i == 0 && j == 0 ? 2.0 : 1.0) / (0.02 + abs(viewZ(uv + o) - z0));","-    sum += texture2D(tAO, uv + o).r * w;","+    ao += texture2D(tAO, uv + o).r * w;","+    if (refl) rf += texture2D(tSSR, uv + o) * w;","     wsum += w;","   }","-  return sum / wsum;","+  ao /= wsum; rf /= wsum;"," }"," "," float hash(vec3 p) { p = fract(p * 0.3183099 + 0.1); p *= 17.0; return fract(p.x * p.y * p.z * (p.x + p.y + p.z)); }"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0fc81173-55a9-40a2-ad78-1a8caf7b8a80","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow","branch":"hedgerow-poc","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.gi