{"parentUuid":"0dddbaf2-74f3-410a-aa8d-c00b4bffee2b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ca86ac74-b393-4b38-8e69-5ddecc3498f5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Z57bg5LBc7xAuFjhsafAu","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"83de309b-b190-49f7-a169-0e247ccf1f6d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T11:34:08.430Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/volumetric.js","oldString":"    setSSR(ssr, strength = 1) {\n      u.tSSR.value = ssr ? ssr.texture : null;\n      u.uSSR.value = ssr ? strength : 0;\n    },","newString":"    setSSR(ssr, strength = 1) {\n      u.tSSR.value = ssr ? ssr.texture : null;\n      u.uSSR.value = ssr ? strength : 0;\n      if (ssr && !u.tAO.value) u.uAOTexel.value = ssr.texel;\n    },","originalFile":"/* Hedgerow — light in the rain.\n\n   A pass for `renderer.setEffects`, first in the chain (it reads the\n   scene's depth): the glow that lamps, fires, muzzle flashes and\n   explosions put into the wet air between the camera and whatever each\n   pixel sees. For a point light in an even medium the light scattered\n   towards the eye along a view ray has a closed form (the \"airlight\"\n   integral): with the ray's closest approach to the light at distance h\n   and parameter t0, the inverse-square falloff integrates to\n       (atan((t1 - t0) / h) - atan((ta - t0) / h)) / h\n   over the stretch [ta, t1] of the ray inside the light's range, and that\n   stretch ends at the surface the pixel shows — so a wall in front of a\n   lamp hides the lamp's glow behind it, and a soldier walking past a fire\n   cuts a dark shape out of its haze. A forward-leaning phase function\n   makes lights ahead of the camera glow more than those behind it, and a\n   slow noise drifting with the wind breaks the haze into rain curtains.\n   Up to eight of the strongest lights near the camera (the light pool's\n   choice, lights.js) take part each frame.\n\n   It also lays the ambient occlusion of ssao.js and the reflections of\n   ssr.js onto the scene first: both half-resolution, brought up with one\n   depth-aware 3 x 3 filter (so they do not bleed across edges). The\n   occlusion spares bright pixels — lamps, fires and lit windows are not\n   darkened by what is near them — and so do the reflections, which take\n   the place of what the material reflected (the sky) in proportion to how\n   mirror-like the scene pass says the pixel is (its alpha). */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\n\nconst MAX = 8;\n\nconst VERT = /* glsl */ `\nvarying vec2 vUv;\nvoid main() { vUv = uv; gl_Position = vec4(position.xy, 0.0, 1.0); }`;\n\nconst FRAG = /* glsl */ `\n#define MAX ${MAX}\nuniform sampler2D tSrc;\nuniform sampler2D tDepth;\nuniform mat4 uProjInv, uViewInv;\nuniform vec3 uCam;\nuniform vec3 uPos[MAX];\nuniform vec3 uCol[MAX];\nuniform float uRange[MAX];\nuniform int uCount;\nuniform float uDensity, uTime, uRain, uFar;\nuniform vec2 uWind;\nuniform sampler2D tAO, tSSR;\nuniform vec2 uAOTexel;\nuniform float uAO, uSSR;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\n\nfloat viewZ(vec2 uv) {\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, uv).x;\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(uv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  return v.z / v.w;\n}\n// the half-resolution layers brought up to full size, weighted by depth likeness\nvoid layers(vec2 uv, float z0, bool refl, out float ao, out vec4 rf) {\n  float wsum = 0.0;\n  ao = 0.0; rf = vec4(0.0);\n  for (int j = -1; j <= 1; j++) for (int i = -1; i <= 1; i++) {\n    vec2 o = vec2(float(i), float(j)) * uAOTexel;\n    float w = (i == 0 && j == 0 ? 2.0 : 1.0) / (0.02 + abs(viewZ(uv + o) - z0));\n    ao += texture2D(tAO, uv + o).r * w;\n    if (refl) rf += texture2D(tSSR, uv + o) * w;\n    wsum += w;\n  }\n  ao /= wsum; rf /= wsum;\n}\n\nfloat hash(vec3 p) { p = fract(p * 0.3183099 + 0.1); p *= 17.0; return fract(p.x * p.y * p.z * (p.x + p.y + p.z)); }\nfloat noise(vec3 x) {\n  vec3 i = floor(x), f = fract(x);\n  f = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f);\n  return mix(mix(mix(hash(i), hash(i + vec3(1, 0, 0)), f.x), mix(hash(i + vec3(0, 1, 0)), hash(i + vec3(1, 1, 0)), f.x), f.y),\n             mix(mix(hash(i + vec3(0, 0, 1)), hash(i + vec3(1, 0, 1)), f.x), mix(hash(i + vec3(0, 1, 1)), hash(i + vec3(1, 1, 1)), f.x), f.y), f.z);\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n  vec4 src = texture2D(tSrc, vUv);\n  vec3 col = src.rgb;\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, vUv).x;\n  // the view ray and the distance to what this pixel shows\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(vUv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  v.xyz /= v.w;\n  float T = d >= 1.0 ? uFar : min(length(v.xyz), uFar);\n  // how mirror-like the scene pass says this pixel is (mirrorAlpha in terrain.js)\n  float mirror = uSSR * clamp(1.0 - src.a * 4.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n  if ((uAO > 0.0 || mirror > 0.0) && d < 1.0) {\n    float ao; vec4 rf;\n    layers(vUv, v.z, mirror > 0.0, ao, rf);\n    float lum = dot(col, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722));\n    col *= mix(1.0, ao, uAO * (1.0 - smoothstep(0.8, 5.0, lum)));\n    if (rf.a > 1e-4) col = mix(col, rf.rgb / rf.a, rf.a * mirror * (1.0 - smoothstep(1.5, 6.0, lum)));\n  }\n  vec3 dir = normalize(mat3(uViewInv) * v.xyz);\n  vec3 add = vec3(0.0);\n  for (int i = 0; i < MAX; i++) {\n    if (i >= uCount) break;\n    vec3 L = uPos[i] - uCam;\n    float t0 = dot(L, dir);\n    float h2 = max(dot(L, L) - t0 * t0, 0.0);\n    float R = uRange[i];\n    if (h2 > R * R) continue;\n    // the stretch of the ray inside the light's range, cut by the surface\n    float w = sqrt(R * R - h2);\n    float ta = max(0.0, t0 - w), tb = min(T, t0 + w);\n    if (tb <= ta) continue;\n    float h = sqrt(h2) + 0.35;                 // a soft core: no singularity at the bulb\n    float I = (atan((tb - t0) / h) - atan((ta - t0) / h)) / h;\n    // fade towards the edge of the range like the light itself\n    float edge = 1.0 - smoothstep(0.55, 1.0, sqrt(h2) / R);\n    // forward scattering (Henyey-Greenstein, g = 0.45) seen from the closest point\n    float c = t0 / max(length(L), 1e-3);\n    float g = 0.45;\n    float phase = 0.0795775 * (1.0 - g * g) / pow(1.0 + g * g - 2.0 * g * c, 1.5);\n    // rain curtains drifting with the wind, round the closest point of approach\n    vec3 q = uCam + dir * clamp(t0, ta, tb);\n    float n = noise(vec3(q.x * 0.35 + uWind.x * uTime, q.y * 0.18 - uTime * 0.9, q.z * 0.35 + uWind.y * uTime));\n    add += uCol[i] * I * edge * phase * (0.55 + 0.9 * n);\n  }\n  col += add * uDensity * (0.6 + 0.4 * uRain);\n  gl_FragColor = vec4(col, 1.0);\n}`;\n\nexport function createVolumetric(camera) {\n  const geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n  geometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([-1, 3, 0, -1, -1, 0, 3, -1, 0], 3));\n  geometry.setAttribute('uv', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([0, 2, 0, 0, 2, 0], 2));\n  const material = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({\n    vertexShader: VERT, fragmentShader: FRAG,\n    uniforms: {\n      tSrc: { value: null }, tDepth: { value: null },\n      uProjInv: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() }, uViewInv: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() },\n      uCam: { value: new THREE.Vector3() },\n      uPos: { value: Array.from({ length: MAX }, () => new THREE.Vector3()) },\n      uCol: { value: Array.from({ length: MAX }, () => new THREE.Vector3()) },\n      uRange: { value: new Array(MAX).fill(1) },\n      uCount: { value: 0 },\n      uDensity: { value: 0.03 }, uTime: { value: 0 }, uRain: { value: 1 }, uFar: { value: 140 },\n      uWind: { value: new THREE.Vector2(0.5, 0.2) },\n      tAO: { value: null }, uAOTexel: { value: new THREE.Vector2(1, 1) }, uAO: { value: 0 },\n      tSSR: { value: null }, uSSR: { value: 0 },\n    },\n    depthTest: false, depthWrite: false, toneMapped: false,\n  });\n  const quad = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);\n  quad.frustumCulled = false;\n  const ortho = new THREE.OrthographicCamera(-1, 1, 1, -1, 0, 1);\n  const u = material.uniforms;\n\n  return {\n    enabled: true, needsSwap: true, uniforms: u,\n    /* this frame's lights: [{x, y, z, color, intensity, range}] */\n    setLights(list, time, rain = 1) {\n      const n = Math.min(MAX, list.length);\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        const l = list[i];\n        u.uPos.value[i].set(l.x, l.y, l.z);\n        u.uCol.value[i].set(l.color.r, l.color.g, l.color.b).multiplyScalar(l.intensity);\n        u.uRange.value[i] = l.range * 0.8;\n      }\n      u.uCount.value = n;\n      u.uTime.value = time;\n      u.uRain.value = rain;\n    },\n    /* the occlusion pass to apply (ssao.js), and how strongly (0: none) */\n    setAO(ssao, strength = 0.85) {\n      u.tAO.value = ssao ? ssao.texture : null;\n      u.uAOTexel.value = ssao ? ssao.uniforms.uTexel.value : u.uAOTexel.value;\n      u.uAO.value = ssao ? strength : 0;\n    },\n    /* the reflections pass to lay on (ssr.js, at the occlusion's half\n       resolution: the upsample shares its texel), and how strongly */\n    setSSR(ssr, strength = 1) {\n      u.tSSR.value = ssr ? ssr.texture : null;\n      u.uSSR.value = ssr ? strength : 0;\n    },\n    render(renderer, writeBuffer, readBuffer) {\n      if (!readBuffer.depthTexture) { this.enabled = false; return; }\n      camera.updateMatrixWorld();\n      u.uProjInv.value.copy(camera.projectionMatrixInverse);\n      u.uViewInv.value.copy(camera.matrixWorld);\n      u.uCam.value.setFromMatrixPosition(camera.matrixWorld);\n      u.tSrc.value = readBuffer.texture;\n      u.tDepth.value = readBuffer.depthTexture;\n      renderer.setRenderTarget(writeBuffer);\n      renderer.render(quad, ortho);\n    },\n  };\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":176,"oldLines":6,"newStart":176,"newLines":7,"lines":["     setSSR(ssr, strength = 1) {","       u.tSSR.value = ssr ? ssr.texture : null;","       u.uSSR.value = ssr ? strength : 0;","+      if (ssr && !u.tAO.value) u.uAOTexel.value = ssr.texel;","     },","     render(renderer, writeBuffer, readBuffer) {","       if (!readBuffer.depthTexture) { this.enabled = false; return; }"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"49ac9375-571d-4f83-a3ed-c07fa9c3bfb4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","root":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow","branch":"hedgerow-poc","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0dddbaf2-74f3-410a-aa8d-c00b4bffee2b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"d06ec9ef-a5bf-4d30-8707-52e391dfb976","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ca86ac74-b393-4b38-8e69-5ddecc3498f5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NMfNnyMEWkFsD49sGKNtcy","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/ssr.js has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"ec01cd11-59aa-4368-a43b-c8d030a2e401","timestamp":"2026-10-21T11:34:08.458Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/ssr.js","oldString":"  const u = material.uniforms;\n\n  return {\n    enabled: true, needsSwap: false, uniforms: u, texture: target.texture,\n    setSize(w, h) {\n      target.setSize(Math.max(1, Math.round(w * scale)), Math.max(1, Math.round(h * scale)));\n      u.uTexel.value.set(1 / w, 1 / h);\n    },","newString":"  const u = material.uniforms;\n  const texel = new THREE.Vector2(1, 1);\n\n  return {\n    enabled: true, needsSwap: false, uniforms: u, texture: target.texture,\n    texel,                // of the half-resolution target, for the upsample\n    setSize(w, h) {\n      const tw = Math.max(1, Math.round(w * scale)), th = Math.max(1, Math.round(h * scale));\n      target.setSize(tw, th);\n      texel.set(1 / tw, 1 / th);\n      u.uTexel.value.set(1 / w, 1 / h);\n    },","originalFile":"/* Hedgerow — reflections in the wet street.\n\n   A pass for `renderer.setEffects`, next to the occlusion ahead of the\n   light-in-the-rain pass and, like it, without a swap: it fills its own\n   half-resolution target, which volumetric.js lays over the scene with an\n   upsample that respects depth edges. The scene pass leaves in its alpha\n   how mirror-like each pixel is (terrain.js and materials.js write it from\n   the wet roughness, `mirrorAlpha`: a puddle or the river is a mirror, wet\n   cobbles a dull sheen, everything else nothing). For those pixels a ray\n   goes from the surface along the reflected view direction through the\n   depth buffer — 24 growing steps, then a binary search for the crossing —\n   and what the screen shows at the crossing is the reflection: lit\n   windows, lamps, the houses opposite, a soldier walking past. Standing\n   water lies level and the rain rings of terrain.js ruffle it; a rough\n   film scatters its rays round the mirror direction, which at a low angle\n   stretches the reflection into the long streaks of a wet road. Where the\n   ray leaves the screen or finds nothing the material's own reflection of\n   the sky stays. Fresnel-weighted, faded towards the edges of the screen. */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\nimport { GLSL_HELPERS } from './terrain.js';\n\nconst STEPS = 24;\n\nconst VERT = /* glsl */ `\nvarying vec2 vUv;\nvoid main() { vUv = uv; gl_Position = vec4(position.xy, 0.0, 1.0); }`;\n\nconst FRAG = /* glsl */ `\n#define STEPS ${STEPS}\nuniform sampler2D tSrc, tDepth;\nuniform mat4 uProj, uProjInv, uView, uViewInv;\nuniform vec2 uTexel;\nuniform float uTime, uRain;\nvarying vec2 vUv;\n${GLSL_HELPERS}\n\nvec3 viewPos(vec2 uv) {\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, uv).x;\n  vec4 v = uProjInv * vec4(uv * 2.0 - 1.0, d * 2.0 - 1.0, 1.0);\n  return v.xyz / v.w;\n}\n// view-space z of what the screen shows at uv (the far plane for the sky)\nfloat viewZ(vec2 uv) { return -uProj[3][2] / (texture2D(tDepth, uv).x * 2.0 - 1.0 + uProj[2][2]); }\nvec2 toScreen(vec3 p) { vec4 c = uProj * vec4(p, 1.0); return c.xy / c.w * 0.5 + 0.5; }\nfloat ign(vec2 p) { return fract(52.9829189 * fract(dot(p, vec2(0.06711056, 0.00583715)))); }\n\nvoid main() {\n  float mirror = clamp(1.0 - texture2D(tSrc, vUv).a * 4.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n  float d = texture2D(tDepth, vUv).x;\n  if (mirror < 0.03 || d >= 1.0) { gl_FragColor = vec4(0.0); return; }\n  vec3 P = viewPos(vUv);\n  // the surface normal from the depth (the side with the smaller step keeps edges clean)\n  vec3 px = viewPos(vUv + vec2(uTexel.x, 0.0)) - P, nx = P - viewPos(vUv - vec2(uTexel.x, 0.0));\n  vec3 py = viewPos(vUv + vec2(0.0, uTexel.y)) - P, ny = P - viewPos(vUv - vec2(0.0, uTexel.y));\n  vec3 n = normalize(cross(abs(px.z) < abs(nx.z) ? px : nx, abs(py.z) < abs(ny.z) ? py : ny));\n  if (dot(n, P) > 0.0) n = -n;\n  vec3 nW = mat3(uViewInv) * n;\n  if (nW.y < 0.55) { gl_FragColor = vec4(0.0); return; }   // only what faces the sky holds water\n  vec3 W = (uViewInv * vec4(P, 1.0)).xyz;\n  // standing water lies level; the rain rings ruffle it (the rings terrain.js draws)\n  float pool = smoothstep(0.6, 0.95, mirror);\n  nW = normalize(mix(nW, vec3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0), pool));\n  vec2 rip = rainRipples(W.xz * 1.7, uTime) * uRain * pool;\n  // a rough film scatters the rays round the mirror direction\n  float j = ign(gl_FragCoord.xy);\n  vec2 sc = (vec2(j, ign(gl_FragCoord.yx + 17.0)) - 0.5) * (1.0 - mirror) * 0.24;\n  nW = normalize(nW + vec3(rip.x * 0.06 + sc.x, 0.0, rip.y * 0.06 + sc.y));\n  n = normalize(mat3(uView) * nW);\n  vec3 V = normalize(P);\n  vec3 R = reflect(V, n);\n  // rays turned down into the ground, or back past the camera, find nothing on screen\n  if ((mat3(uViewInv) * R).y < 0.005) { gl_FragColor = vec4(0.0); return; }\n  float facing = 1.0 - smoothstep(-0.15, 0.2, R.z);\n  if (facing <= 0.0) { gl_FragColor = vec4(0.0); return; }\n\n  float dist = -P.z;\n  vec3 O = P + n * (0.02 + dist * 0.002);\n  float stp = 0.05 + dist * 0.01;\n  float t = stp * j, tPrev = 0.0;\n  vec2 hit = vec2(-1.0);\n  float found = 0.0;\n  for (int i = 0; i < STEPS; i++) {\n    tPrev = t;\n    t += stp;\n    vec3 Q = O + R * t;\n    if (Q.z > -0.05) break;\n    vec2 uv = toScreen(Q);\n    if (uv.x < 0.0 || uv.x > 1.0 || uv.y < 0.0 || uv.y > 1.0) break;\n    float dz = viewZ(uv) - Q.z;\n    // behind what the screen shows, but not far behind (or it passed behind a thin thing);\n    // and clearly above the water (not the next bump of the same ground)\n    if (dz > 0.0 && dz < stp * 1.5 + 0.25 && (uViewInv * vec4(Q, 1.0)).y - W.y > 0.12) {\n      float a = tPrev, b = t;\n      for (int k = 0; k < 5; k++) {\n        float m = 0.5 * (a + b);\n        vec3 M = O + R * m;\n        if (viewZ(toScreen(M)) - M.z > 0.0) b = m; else a = m;\n      }\n      hit = toScreen(O + R * b);\n      // the last steps are long: fade rather than cut off where the march ends\n      found = 1.0 - smoothstep(float(STEPS) - 6.0, float(STEPS), float(i));\n      break;\n    }\n    stp *= 1.18;\n  }\n  if (found <= 0.0) { gl_FragColor = vec4(0.0); return; }\n  vec3 c = texture2D(tSrc, hit).rgb;\n  vec2 e = smoothstep(vec2(0.0), vec2(0.06, 0.1), hit) * (1.0 - smoothstep(vec2(0.94, 0.88), vec2(1.0), hit));\n  float F = 0.02 + 0.98 * pow(1.0 - max(dot(n, -V), 0.0), 5.0);\n  float w = F * found * facing * e.x * e.y;\n  // premultiplied, so the upsample averages it right\n  gl_FragColor = vec4(c * w, w);\n}`;\n\nexport function createSSR(camera, shared, { scale = 0.5 } = {}) {\n  const geometry = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n  geometry.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([-1, 3, 0, -1, -1, 0, 3, -1, 0], 3));\n  geometry.setAttribute('uv', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute([0, 2, 0, 0, 2, 0], 2));\n  const material = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({\n    vertexShader: VERT, fragmentShader: FRAG,\n    uniforms: {\n      tSrc: { value: null }, tDepth: { value: null },\n      uProj: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() }, uProjInv: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() },\n      uView: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() }, uViewInv: { value: new THREE.Matrix4() },\n      uTexel: { value: new THREE.Vector2(1 / 1024, 1 / 768) },\n      uTime: shared.time, uRain: shared.rain,\n    },\n    depthTest: false, depthWrite: false, toneMapped: false,\n  });\n  const quad = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, material);\n  quad.frustumCulled = false;\n  const ortho = new THREE.OrthographicCamera(-1, 1, 1, -1, 0, 1);\n  const target = new THREE.WebGLRenderTarget(4, 4, { type: THREE.HalfFloatType, depthBuffer: false, stencilBuffer: false });\n  target.texture.minFilter = target.texture.magFilter = THREE.LinearFilter;\n  const u = material.uniforms;\n\n  return {\n    enabled: true, needsSwap: false, uniforms: u, texture: target.texture,\n    setSize(w, h) {\n      target.setSize(Math.max(1, Math.round(w * scale)), Math.max(1, Math.round(h * scale)));\n      u.uTexel.value.set(1 / w, 1 / h);\n    },\n    render(renderer, writeBuffer, readBuffer) {\n      if (!readBuffer.depthTexture) { this.enabled = false; return; }\n      camera.updateMatrixWorld();\n      u.uProj.value.copy(camera.projectionMatrix);\n      u.uProjInv.value.copy(camera.projectionMatrixInverse);\n      u.uView.value.copy(camera.matrixWorldInverse);\n      u.uViewInv.value.copy(camera.matrixWorld);\n      u.tSrc.value = readBuffer.texture;\n      u.tDepth.value = readBuffer.depthTexture;\n      const prev = renderer.getRenderTarget();\n      renderer.setRenderTarget(target);\n      renderer.render(quad, ortho);\n      renderer.setRenderTarget(prev);\n    },\n  };\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":134,"oldLines":11,"newStart":134,"newLines":15,"lines":["   const target = new THREE.WebGLRenderTarget(4, 4, { type: THREE.HalfFloatType, depthBuffer: false, stencilBuffer: false });","   target.texture.minFilter = target.texture.magFilter = THREE.LinearFilter;","   const u = material.uniforms;","+  const texel = new THREE.Vector2(1, 1);"," ","   return {","     enabled: true, needsSwap: false, uniforms: u, texture: target.texture,","+    texel,                // of the half-resolution target, for the upsample","     setSize(w, h) {","-      target.setSize(Math.max(1, Math.round(w * scale)), Math.max(1, Math.round(h * scale)));","+      const tw = Math.max(1, Math.round(w * scale)), th = Math.max(1, Math.round(h * scale));","+      target.setSize(tw, th);","+      texel.set(1 / tw, 1 / th);","       u.uTexel.value.set(1 / w, 1 / h);","     },","     render(renderer, writeBuffer, readBuffer) {"]}],"userModified":false,"rep