{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"89f1ed43820c2d919078d47a18468d36d46d4c5328705d76d32055c4373ec4f8","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the issue: the old mask spreads water too evenly, making roughness uniform instead of letting puddles form naturally. I'll rebuild standing water as a height-based fill using slow noise, so joints and hollows fill first and deeper areas form real puddles over the stones.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B5C6pWBGrVfpctx8R6XzC5","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/terrain.js","old_string":"        // puddles: the low parts of mud and road, more where the macro noise says so\n        float wetLow = (b.x + b.w * 0.6) * (1.0 - rockW);\n        float pMask = smoothstep(0.42, 0.7, texture2D(tForest, vWPos.xz / 31.0).a * 0.7 + (1.0 - hts.x) * 0.5);\n        tPuddle = wetLow * smoothstep(0.35, 0.55, pMask - nb.w * 0.1 + (1.0 - hts.x) * 0.25) * uWet;","new_string":"        // standing water: a slow noise says where it gathers, and there it\n        // fills the ground up to a level — the joints between the cobbles and\n        // the hollows of the mud first, then (deeper) over the stones too; the\n        // road's joints hold a little everywhere. Not on grass or rock.\n        float hold = (b.x + b.w + b.z * 0.35) * (1.0 - rockW);\n        float gather = texture2D(tForest, vWPos.xz / 31.0).a * 0.65 + texture2D(tMud, vWPos.xz / 9.0).a * 0.35;\n        float level = smoothstep(0.45, 0.75, gather) * 1.2;\n        tPuddle = smoothstep(-0.02, 0.06, level - dot(b, hts));\n        tPuddle = max(tPuddle, b.w * 0.55 * smoothstep(0.32, 0.12, hts.w));\n        tPuddle *= hold * uWet;"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
