{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"8712e5cb-5c17-4f78-8159-fe8e322bd52d","hash":"5d31d5e4022159fd9007bfd0f786eb1300d9ddafe842599f7b8973056322c79c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found that puddles render darker than the surrounding mud because the darkened albedo loses more light than the dim sky reflection provides, making them look wrong at dusk. I'll fix this by having missed reflection rays fall back to screen-space color at their direction's vanishing point (capturing horizon glow, fog, and silhouettes), while still excluding rays occluded by nearby geometry so objects don't incorrectly pick up sky color.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V5ocWy6P8LPV3ZMDj5CJsj","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/ssr.js","old_string":"  float t = stp * j, tPrev = 0.0;\n  vec2 hit = vec2(-1.0);\n  float found = 0.0;\n  for (int i = 0; i < STEPS; i++) {\n    tPrev = t;\n    t += stp;\n    vec3 Q = O + R * t;\n    if (Q.z > -0.05) break;\n    vec2 uv = toScreen(Q);\n    if (uv.x < 0.0 || uv.x > 1.0 || uv.y < 0.0 || uv.y > 1.0) break;\n    float dz = viewZ(uv) - Q.z;\n    // behind what the screen shows, but not far behind (or it passed behind a thin thing);\n    // and clearly above the water (not the next bump of the same ground)\n    if (dz > 0.0 && dz < stp * 1.5 + 0.25 && (uViewInv * vec4(Q, 1.0)).y - W.y > 0.12) {\n      float a = tPrev, b = t;\n      for (int k = 0; k < 5; k++) {\n        float m = 0.5 * (a + b);\n        vec3 M = O + R * m;\n        if (viewZ(toScreen(M)) - M.z > 0.0) b = m; else a = m;\n      }\n      hit = toScreen(O + R * b);\n      // the last steps are long: fade rather than cut off where the march ends\n      found = 1.0 - smoothstep(float(STEPS) - 6.0, float(STEPS), float(i));\n      break;\n    }\n    stp *= 1.18;\n  }\n  if (found <= 0.0) { gl_FragColor = vec4(0.0); return; }","new_string":"  float t = stp * j, tPrev = 0.0;\n  vec2 hit = vec2(-1.0);\n  float found = 0.0;\n  bool blocked = false;\n  for (int i = 0; i < STEPS; i++) {\n    tPrev = t;\n    t += stp;\n    vec3 Q = O + R * t;\n    if (Q.z > -0.05) break;\n    vec2 uv = toScreen(Q);\n    if (uv.x < 0.0 || uv.x > 1.0 || uv.y < 0.0 || uv.y > 1.0) break;\n    float dz = viewZ(uv) - Q.z;\n    if (dz > 0.0) {\n      // behind what the screen shows, but not far behind (or it passed behind a thin thing);\n      // and clearly above the water (not the next bump of the same ground)\n      if (dz < stp * 1.5 + 0.25 && (uViewInv * vec4(Q, 1.0)).y - W.y > 0.12) {\n        float a = tPrev, b = t;\n        for (int k = 0; k < 5; k++) {\n          float m = 0.5 * (a + b);\n          vec3 M = O + R * m;\n          if (viewZ(toScreen(M)) - M.z > 0.0) b = m; else a = m;\n        }\n        hit = toScreen(O + R * b);\n        // the last steps are long: fade rather than cut off where the march ends\n        found = 1.0 - smoothstep(float(STEPS) - 6.0, float(STEPS), float(i));\n        break;\n      }\n      blocked = true;\n    }\n    stp *= 1.18;\n  }\n  // nothing near in the way: the sky and far scenery in the mirror direction\n  // are on screen where that direction vanishes (if they are), as the\n  // camera sees them — the glow over the horizon, far roofs, lightning\n  if (found <= 0.0 && !blocked) {\n    vec4 cv = uProj * vec4(R, 0.0);\n    vec2 uvInf = cv.xy / max(cv.w, 1e-4) * 0.5 + 0.5;\n    if (cv.w > 0.0 && uvInf.x > 0.0 && uvInf.x < 1.0 && uvInf.y > 0.0 && uvInf.y < 1.0 && viewZ(uvInf) < -60.0) {\n      hit = uvInf;\n      found = 1.0;\n    }\n  }\n  if (found <= 0.0) { gl_FragColor = vec4(0.0); return; }"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CCLyjrkNTWBHnJQZJ9R4fn","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow/fun/hedgerow/js/ssr.js","old_string":"   stretches the reflection into the long streaks of a wet road. Where the\n   ray leaves the screen or finds nothing the material's own reflection of\n   the sky stays. Fresnel-weighted, faded towards the edges of the screen. */","new_string":"   stretches the reflection into the long streaks of a wet road. A ray that\n   meets nothing near reflects what the camera sees where its direction\n   vanishes on screen, when that is far (the sky, the glow over the\n   horizon, the far roofs); one that leaves the screen, or passed behind\n   something, keeps the material's own reflection of the sky. Fresnel-\n   weighted, faded towards the edges of the screen. */"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TDnzTDPiY7AnbmnfKkUfaC","name":"mcp__Claude_Browser__javascript_tool","input":{"action":"javascript_exec","text":"location.reload();","tabId":"seed"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HyFwnpCzAdbw3QotCHnZPz","name":"mcp__Claude_Browser__javascript_tool","input":{"action":"javascript_exec","text":"await (0, eval)(sessionStorage.h);\nawait ready();\nawait go(1.0, -12, 0, -0.1, 1.7, 2000);\nconst U = window.hedgerow.fx.volumetric.uniforms;\nawait snap('r6_lane2');\nU.uSSR.value = 0; await snap('r6_lane2_off'); U.uSSR.value = 1;\nawait go(0, 96, 0, -0.02, 1.7, 1500);\nawait snap('r6_street4');\n'ok'","tabId":"seed"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017aZPjDrG6n8CpMxC5FrnMu","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"REDACTED.jpg"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
